WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.020
Live from Atlantis The Palm,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:26.580
in the presence of some of the biggest
and brightest stars in world football.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.880
Welcome to Dubai.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.540
Distinguished guests,

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:39.620
ladies and gentlemen, football fans,
good evening and welcome one and all.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.780
Whether you're here in the room or
of course, tuning in from across the globe

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.700
to this, the 18th annual
Dubai International Sports conference,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.500
as well as the 14th edition of the Dubai
Globe Soccer Award straight afterwards.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.100
This one's organized annually
by the Dubai Sports Council.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.540
Been doing this since 2006.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:02.880
The Dubai International Sports Conference,
which is a member of the

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:06.740
Mohammed Bin Rashid Al Maktoum Global initiatives,
has delivered many,

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:11.980
many substantial debates driven
by the biggest names in the game.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:17.100
They come to engage in discussions around
topics, topics which explore various

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.930
aspects that make football
the global phenomenon that it is.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.210
So why are we here tonight?

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.780
Well, the theme of our discussion this

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.290
evening centers around sustainability and,
of course, performance in football.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.260
While on the topic of sustainability,

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:37.260
we here at the Dubai Sports Council
and the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.850
recognize the extraordinary importance
of environmental responsibility.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:46.900
And we are committed to measuring
the emissions associated with this event.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.850
Recognizing that responsibility,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.020
we are committed to offsetting all
the measured emissions and of course,

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:59.020
taking further steps to eventually ensure
a carbon neutral event in the future.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:03.420
So, without further ado,
it is time to get things started.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.060
We're ready.
You're ready.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.020
And facilitating this year's conference,

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.450
it is, of course, sports anchor from our

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.860
media father, CNN,
please welcome Amanda Davies.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.120
Thank you very much indeed, Tom.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.580
Welcome, everybody.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:25.660
They say the hardest thing when you reach
the top is to stay at the top, don't they?

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:28.300
Perhaps a clichê, but it is true.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.610
And there are not many in football

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:36.020
who have done it as consistently for such
a period of time as the gentlemen there,

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.960
who'll join us to share some of the secrets

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.820
of their success over
the next 30 minutes or so.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.940
We are talking reaching peak performance

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:48.940
and sustaining it,
sustaining the beautiful game.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.340
So let's crack on.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.660
Please welcome two players integral

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:58.540
to last season's history making
campaign by Manchester City.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.020
Firstly, a portuguese international

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:06.460
with 53 caps for his country,
consistently named in the FIFPro World XI

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.900
for his role in City's back line.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.260
So integral to that european treble

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:20.420
winning season, it is Ruben Dias.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.920
Welcome.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.340
Next up, a player who joins him
in that back line, a fullback who's helped

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:41.900
City to five Premier League
titles since he joined in 2017.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:46.360
As well as that incredible success last
year, known as one of the best fullbacks

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.540
of a generation, known for his pace,
strength and vision.

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.760
Ladies and gentlemen, Kyle Walker.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.460
So that leaves us with one chair

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:14.660
and joining the Manchester City duo
a player in his 22nd season as

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:19.420
a professional footballer who spent
most of those as part of the GOATs.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.860
The Greatest Of All Time
debate.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:24.300
A five time Champions League winner,

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:29.220
the top goal scorer of all time
and showing no sign of slowing down,

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.580
having topped the world goal
scoring charts last year.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.480
Please welcome Cristiano Ronaldo.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.020
Amazing.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.540
Thank you so much
for your time, gentlemen.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:03.940
I mean, Cristiano, you've made no secret
of your Manchester United allegiance,

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.700
meaning you'd have a bit of a problem,
perhaps, moving to City,

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:14.760
but are you at least able to
appreciate the success and what they've

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.900
done in the last twelve months?
It was amazing.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.900
First of all, good evening
or good night for everybody.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.140
I'm so pleased to be here.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.660
Thank you for the welcome.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.060
Well, about them.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.180
Amazing season.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.180
Congratulations to Manchester City
for them and all players.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:37.700
The coach, they did amazing work
and finally they win the Champions League.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:41.300
In my opinion, they should deserve to win,

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.380
maybe two years ago,

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:51.300
but the timing always come and to be
honest, I enjoy to watch them to play.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:57.220
I think they have a very good team, very
good coach, the system, how they play.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.380
So amazing.
Congratulations.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.420
Yeah.
And that doesn't come easily, I guess.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.740
From you, nothing is easy.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:06.080
They deserve.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.900
Ruben, so much had been made about

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:16.140
the weight and so close,
yet so far for you in the City team.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:21.600
What psychologically did it
mean to get over that line?

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:28.620
Well, I think until you actually do it,
you've not done it.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.140
But also I think that,
especially when we're talking about a club

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:37.220
that has done it for the first time,
it takes a process to do that.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.580
So, in the end, today,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:45.700
you see these faces collecting the big
award, but it's been a work of many years.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:50.840
And in the end, it's not just us,
it's a whole process.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.420
And the congratulations,
it's obviously for us, but for all

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:59.820
the guys that participated before,
managers, players, everyone involved,

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:04.800
because to bring the club to where it was,
to where it is now,

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:08.180
I think that's the biggest
prize we all have.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.820
Kyle, what is the secret of the success?

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:15.900
I mean, this is the point in the season
where you're looking from the outside,

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:21.980
people waiting for the leaders to have
a wobble, to make a few mistakes.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:25.300
This is where City
cranks through the gears.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.860
Yeah.
I mean, in recent years,

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:32.740
we've known to kick on after the Christmas
period,

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:37.540
but I think what the key and the secret
is wanting to do it again and again.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:41.300
I think the manager is
a massive driving force in that.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:46.060
But I think also some of the players
that we've brought in took out.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:48.460
We've always made sure that we've kept

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.260
the high standards and made sure
that we keep winning year after year.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:58.720
And Pep very openly said, this is
not just about one Champions League crown.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:00.660
You've got to go on and win it again.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:03.540
Cristiano, that is something
that you did with Real Madrid.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:06.780
Not just once, but twice, but three times.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.940
What was the key in that, do you think?

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.300
The key.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:14.900
Well, it's difficult to say.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:20.580
I think it's belief, the dedication,

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:25.140
hard work, and in my opinion,

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.300
nothing is a coincidence.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:30.340
So I think they have potential
to do it the same.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.020
I hope no, but they have potential.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:37.340
But I think they have potential
because they still have good team.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.020
Some players,

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:42.400
they are on prime,
they play good football.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:46.580
I think they have a good chance
to win the Champions League again.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:52.380
But we will see many factors will happen.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.340
Who do you see as
the favorites this season?

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:55.060
The favorite?

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:59.400
Yeah,
well, they're always in the top to be

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.980
the favorites, but they're
always the same clubs.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:06.760
Bayern, Manchester City, Real Madrid.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.260
I don't know.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:12.380
I think that three will be
the finals, I think.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.249
Who do you see as the favorites, Kyle?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:19.700
Yeah, I think just there you look at them,

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:23.300
three teams, Bayern Munich,
Real Madrid, Manchester City.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.140
We're all there with good players.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:28.100
You know, who've a chance
of winning it, you'd say.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.940
But I also feel that you need luck.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:30.960
You need a little bit of luck

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.300
in the Champions League to make sure
that you get to the final and then it's

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:38.860
down for big players and big moments
to then also go and win you that game,

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:42.300
which we've got a lot
in the dressing room.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.660
Obviously, I'm sat next to him
and he's a fantastic player.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:48.140
One of the best that's
ever graced the game.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:52.980
But I think what's very key with our
team is that there's no standout.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.220
We're all a collective and we're a team,

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.260
and we rely on each other to make
sure that we can get over the line.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.860
We look at the other night and Kevin's

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:06.420
come on on the 70th minute and obviously
the capabilities that Kevin has and stuff

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:11.380
like that, but it's a process, it's a team
game and that's what we're in it for.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.942
And we make sure that we
get to places where we can, for a collective.

00:10:15.943 --> 00:10:18.860
Cristiano,
it's a team game, without doubt.

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:25.220
But there was all eyes on you as one
player when you made the move to Saudi.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.620
I think it's fair to say there were a few

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:31.100
people who weren't
the most positive about it.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:38.600
But how did that act
for you as a motivation?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:45.660
Well, I thought will be a good move to me.
Why not

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:48.180
to give a chance to another countries

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.900
with my football,
with my passion, to change mentalities?

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:53.140
Why not?

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.320
And I'm capable to do that.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.660
I'm not be arrogant,
but I said that one year ago.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.660
The things change, the world change,

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:05.860
the football change,
the rules change, everything change.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:09.020
So my move, I think it was a good move.

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:10.380
I feel so happy.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:13.900
Many players move there, coaches,

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:17.900
directors, even nutritionists,
they moving there.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:22.060
So the Saudi is in the process.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.500
That will take long.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:29.100
But in a life we always say step
by step we reach to the highest level.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:35.260
So I believe they're going to be
in the top three-four in the world.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.800
But step by step I think
we're going to reach that.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.540
Where do you think the level is now?

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.860
You're a year on, aren't you?

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:51.180
You're a year on to your
life in Saudi Arabia.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.740
Where do you think the level is now?

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.060
The level right now?

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:59.200
To be honest, I think the Saudi League is

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:03.820
not worse than France's
league to be in my opinion.

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:07.120
And French league I think you have two,

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:10.620
three teams with a good level.
In Saudi now,

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.180
I think it's more competitive.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:13.500
They can say whatever they want.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:17.660
It's just my opinion and I played there one
year so I know what I'm talking about.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:24.420
But I think right now we are better
than France League, so we still improve.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:29.180
What do you think is the key in terms
of taking it to the next level?

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:34.620
The key, you have many factors that apply
to improve the league.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:39.300
As I say before,
they have many things to improve.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:46.700
But I think with the powerful people
behind to help to change a little bit

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:52.780
the culture of football, the bad habits,
I think we're going to reach in one point

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:56.420
that the people there
in Saudi will be proud.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.780
The investment there, it's huge.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.780
So why not believe on that?

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.540
Like in Saudi, even in Dubai,

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:09.100
the things change and the world
change so they deserve opportunities.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:12.260
How much did you use
the criticism as motivation?

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.020
Say again?

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:16.020
How much did you use
the criticism as motivation?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.660
It's part of the journey.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:23.220
I'm always dealing with that.
I'm professional 22 years.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:30.580
It's part of my journey to be a better
man, a better player, a better father.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.460
So it's good.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:36.720
I like when the people doubt about me
and I prove again that

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:42.220
one year with successful I had last
year a little bit difficult journey.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.740
But I'm glad that things happened because

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:52.600
make me feel more strong and you can
see this year I did a fantastic season.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.780
I was the best goal scorer, imagine,

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:02.140
to beat that animals, the young lions,
like Haaland, for example, with the goals.

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:03.340
So I'm proud.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:08.680
I'm 39 soon and I'm still
looking good, so I'm proud.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.580
Ruben, you've had the pleasure,

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:21.620
I'm guessing, of being a teammate
of both Cristiano and Erling.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:23.660
Which would you rather on your team?

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:25.580
Difficult question.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:28.100
Well, in the end, they're
just different players.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:34.300
Obviously, Cristiano is older now,
he's in a different stage of his career.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.940
But obviously,

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:41.500
when it comes to choose between players,
I always stay away from that question,

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:47.100
just because everyone's different and you
have many different ways of seeing

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:51.020
the game these days,
and one might fit best one kind of idea,

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.940
the other one might fit best
the other one.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:59.460
But in the end, I think I wouldn't be
badly served with either of them because

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:02.500
the one thing they both
do a lot is scoring goals.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:07.700
Cristiano was talking about using
criticism and the skeptics as motivation.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:13.020
Thierry Henry recently revealed that he
now looks back and thinks he was suffering

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:19.500
with mental depression and low
points during his career.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:25.900
How do you deal with the tough moments
yet still perform on the pitch?

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:31.580
Well, I think, since young, we're told,
and we grow up knowing that that's

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:36.300
unfortunately part of being a footballer,
especially on the top level.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.900
The more visibility you have,

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:42.740
the more open you are to criticism,
as much as you are also open to when

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:46.420
things go well, to get cheered
and beloved by everyone.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:50.260
It's about, I think,
building that strong mindset that will

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:55.420
shield you in a way and protect yourself
when the times get a bit more tough.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.660
And then in the end,

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:00.740
it's about a little bit of fight
with yourself and always coming up on top.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.200
A bit like you were saying,
all of us get criticism in a moment of our

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:09.420
lives for personal matters,
for professional reasons.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:13.380
It can be from whatever side
you might sometimes not expect.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.300
But what does matter is that

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:20.620
you always stay strong and you always
remember where you're going for.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:23.900
And I think in here, in this room,
we have many examples of that.

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:26.380
How much do you rely
on yourself in those moments?

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:29.700
How much do you lean on the team?

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:30.740
I do think that,

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:34.340
especially on those moments of criticism,
is when you most rely on yourself,

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:39.860
is when you most have to rely on
everything you've built yourself with.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:43.540
Because that's the moment where probably
you're not going to have so much people

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.460
around you trying to help
you and supporting you.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.380
And that's the one moment in which you

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:52.500
just grind it out and you show the world
and everyone around you that you're there.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.300
And people can talk,

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:59.740
people can say whatever they want to say,
but you are who you want to be.

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:02.880
Let's talk about Pep.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.840
What is life under Pep Guardiola like?

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.760
It's tough on days.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:18.050
I think I speak for probably everyone now
that for what he's achieved,

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:22.420
what he does in football,
what he teaches you, not just

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:25.050
as a football player,
but as a person.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.380
No pressure, I mean, look at that glare.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.530
No, but he's fantastic
and he probably knows that.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:33.980
But it is tough because he
demands so much from you.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:38.700
But it's also what you should do every day
and come to training and make sure

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:43.460
that you give 100% and you should
demand from yourself as well.

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.940
But sometimes you do have off days,
but you can't have off days with him

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:51.840
because as soon as you have off days,
he's normally shouting at you.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:56.740
Ederson said, the thing with Pep is

00:17:56.770 --> 00:18:00.220
that he's always ten steps ahead
of everybody else.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:04.140
As a player,
how hard is that to keep up with?

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.640
Well, I think

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:11.770
it shouldn't be difficult,
because if there's one thing besides

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:15.140
having the manager we have
and the structure we have,

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:19.050
is that we also have players that want
to be forward as well,

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:24.570
even though sometimes we're not,
and he's the one that keeps on pulling us.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.800
But as a player,
if you're ambitious and if you want

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.290
to keep on winning,
especially after so many great things

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:35.380
that this team has done, this is the kind
of person you need next to you.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:39.740
Obviously, it's an effort of everyone,
not just him, not just us, everyone.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.770
But he's the man in front of the ship,

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.980
so it is crucial that he's
got that mentality.

00:18:46.010 --> 00:18:51.660
How do you compare, Cristiano, what you
see from Pep with Sir Alex Ferguson?

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:57.330
I think the mindset of the winners,
they are different, in my opinion.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.180
Personality, the character,
the way they see the life,

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:04.050
the way they see the players,
the way they see the difficult moments.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:08.570
The top players and top coaches,
they're thinking different.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:12.770
As I say before, no coincidence
that he win what he won.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:16.500
So no miracles, hard work.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:20.090
You see different things that the other
ones, like Sir Alex Ferguson,

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:25.520
and of course other coaches,
too, they are different.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:32.770
And when you look at what happens next

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:39.660
in your career,
what happens next in your career,

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:44.220
how much longer can you
keep this level going?

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.810
I don't know.
I live day by day.

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:51.380
How much do you rely on the data and the
facts and how much of it is instinct?

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:56.330
Listen,
with some issues that I had,

00:19:56.360 --> 00:20:02.420
personal and professional make me feel
and make me thinking in a different way.

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:06.290
As I told you before,
I thinking the present and the moment.

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.660
The moment is good.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:08.940
I feel good.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.660
I still capable to do

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.770
some goals, to help my team,
to help the national team too.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:20.770
So I will carry on.
The moment when I finish?

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.220
I don't know, to be honest.

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:26.810
But of course will be soon.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.460
Soon, I mean, ten years more.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.800
But I'm joking.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:32.050
So relative.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:35.180
It's all relative.
I don't know.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.620
Let's see.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:40.500
Are you instinct or data?
Instinct.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:41.180
Instinct.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:47.700
I feel for me it's more
on just play on how you feel.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.250
I think when you're happy and when you're

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:54.530
feeling happy in yourself,
we're doing the job that everyone loves.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:57.560
Everyone as a small kid playing football.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:59.220
We wanted to do what we're doing now.

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.700
So I just want to enjoy it.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:05.380
I want to enjoy it to the fullest capacity

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.050
and then just play
with a smile on my face.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:12.010
I think for Cristiano, whenever he
wants to retire, he will retire.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.420
He deserves the right of that.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:19.180
But I'm more off instinct and just
doing what makes me happy.

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:23.660
As the calendar gets longer,
Bernardo Silva was very open,

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:27.420
talking about the Club World
Cup and the expansion of that.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:28.620
How easy is that?

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:34.360
How much tougher does it make your
job to keep the level where you are?

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:38.290
I don't think it becomes tougher
because we're doing what we love.

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:41.380
Like I just said before, this is what

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:44.330
we're paid to do and we're
paid well to do it.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:48.330
So to achieve what we've achieved,
I feel we probably should have won

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:52.090
a Champions League before when we
got to the final against Chelsea.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:55.180
But you do need setbacks in life.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.090
You do need things to come back from,

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:02.220
or nearly moments to then also achieve
your dream, which we went unachieved

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:06.780
to then win the Super cup and the
Club World cup after that was a bonus.

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:10.380
You're in them competitions because
you won the Champions League.

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:14.140
So listen, we're in the FA cup,
obviously still fighting very hard

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:16.290
for the Premier League and still
in the Champions League.

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:19.780
So we'll try and replicate
what we did last year.

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:24.420
Who knows what's going
to happen, but why not?

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:28.120
How is your career compared to what you

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:33.940
had hoped for when you were
starting out as a young boy?

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:35.540
Well, to start at Sheffield United

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:42.540
and then go to Tottenham at the age of 19
and leave there at 27 with no medals was

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:46.400
tough.
To come here and won the amount

00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:49.500
of Premier Leagues that I've
won in a short amount of time.

00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:54.420
And obviously the Champions League,
it's been more than ever dreamed of.

00:22:54.450 --> 00:22:57.090
But that's not just me that's without

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:59.940
the past and present
players that have been here.

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:01.180
It's just been a journey,

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:05.420
and it's been a journey that I've loved,
and that's why I've extended my contract,

00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:09.800
obviously, at Manchester City, and it's
a team that's fully in my heart.

00:23:09.830 --> 00:23:12.500
How much of your career,
and I'll ask this to Ruben

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:19.980
as well, how much of your career was
dependent on your academy career and life

00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:26.330
as a schoolboy, and how much has it
been your development subsequently?

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:28.900
I think it teaches you

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:33.570
certain things or certain paths
in your life when you are a schoolboy.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:38.260
I think probably now you look at Rico
and Oscar that are here tonight,

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:42.020
that I think the born old Phil,
who was born in 2000,

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:45.260
that their paths are going to be
completely different to what mine was.

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:47.260
But I think everyone has their journey.

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:50.460
Everyone has their journey in life,
and it's brought us to where we all are

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.660
today, enjoying this moment
and this special night.

00:23:53.690 --> 00:23:56.420
And I just feel what your path is.

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:58.040
It's destiny.

00:23:58.520 --> 00:24:05.380
Ruben, in terms of how much was set when
you were at the academies in Portugal?

00:24:05.410 --> 00:24:08.540
Well, obviously, I guess I consider myself

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:12.620
very fortunate to have been
brought up in Benfica's academy.

00:24:12.650 --> 00:24:17.620
I don't know if people are very aware,
but the academy has probably everything

00:24:17.650 --> 00:24:22.570
a young player can need to become
whatever you want to become.

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:26.180
But I think you can come
from different backgrounds.

00:24:26.210 --> 00:24:30.330
At home, I had a different example,
a very different one, my own brother,

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:36.220
and he was living in another
way of making his own way.

00:24:36.250 --> 00:24:44.400
But I think just being around football
in a way, in a dressing room, dealing with

00:24:44.720 --> 00:24:48.660
other young footballers,
it just helps you develop.

00:24:48.690 --> 00:24:49.740
It helps you.

00:24:49.770 --> 00:24:51.740
I've met many people from different

00:24:51.770 --> 00:24:57.290
backgrounds that just
get a very good shape in terms of just

00:24:57.320 --> 00:25:00.640
getting away from their normal place
and getting into football in which you

00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:03.570
just deal with different communities
and different kinds of people.

00:25:03.600 --> 00:25:04.540
So in the end, yeah,

00:25:04.570 --> 00:25:08.740
I think the final result,
whether you make it to the top or not,

00:25:08.760 --> 00:25:11.570
is always going to be something
better than what you were before.

00:25:11.600 --> 00:25:13.940
Kyle mentioned Rico coming through.

00:25:13.970 --> 00:25:16.290
What do you see as you guys see as your

00:25:16.320 --> 00:25:21.570
role in terms of developing the next
generation and allowing them to flourish

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:24.330
not only in the dressing room,
but on the pitch as well?

00:25:24.360 --> 00:25:26.540
He's actually not that old.

00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:28.380
He just talks like he's 33.

00:25:28.410 --> 00:25:30.380
He's one a lot.

00:25:30.410 --> 00:25:35.090
No, we try and make sure
that it's enjoyable.

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:36.700
You want to come to work and enjoy it.

00:25:36.730 --> 00:25:41.620
First and foremost, me, Kevin,
Ruben, Rodri, Bernardo, the captains.

00:25:41.650 --> 00:25:44.980
We make sure that it's an enjoyable place.

00:25:45.010 --> 00:25:47.700
You come here because you're happy,

00:25:47.730 --> 00:25:51.380
but we're here to win,
and that's the main thing.

00:25:51.410 --> 00:25:56.020
And like Ruben said, it comes
from the driving force as the manager.

00:25:56.050 --> 00:26:00.940
But our job as the captains is
to make sure that the lads are happy.

00:26:00.970 --> 00:26:03.260
The lads are fully focused on what we need

00:26:03.290 --> 00:26:07.260
to do and where this team is shaped from,
is that we're his voice in the changing room.

00:26:07.290 --> 00:26:10.260
And I don't know whether you
saw this week Vinicius Jr.

00:26:10.290 --> 00:26:13.780
scoring his goal
and paying tribute to you.

00:26:13.810 --> 00:26:18.810
How much pride do you take from that in
terms of inspiring the next generation?

00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:23.500
It's good when you have a family,
big family, like I am.

00:26:23.530 --> 00:26:27.020
So it's good to be proud of your kids.

00:26:27.050 --> 00:26:30.500
Junior do it his way.

00:26:30.530 --> 00:26:33.940
I think he have a good talent still,

00:26:33.970 --> 00:26:39.420
to improve more, I need to teach him some
tricks, but I think he's in a good way.

00:26:39.450 --> 00:26:40.900
He's a good boy.

00:26:40.930 --> 00:26:42.460
He like to play football.

00:26:42.490 --> 00:26:43.810
He have the drive.

00:26:43.840 --> 00:26:46.290
So he make me happy.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:49.700
What is your key bit of advice to the next

00:26:49.730 --> 00:26:55.560
generation, in terms of making
it to the top and staying there?

00:26:56.400 --> 00:26:57.810
Believe.

00:26:57.840 --> 00:27:01.380
I think you should believe in everything.

00:27:01.410 --> 00:27:04.700
And, of course, the rest.

00:27:04.730 --> 00:27:07.660
It's the dedication, the hard work.

00:27:07.690 --> 00:27:10.540
Listen to people who know more than you,

00:27:10.570 --> 00:27:16.180
who they have more experience than you,
and believe in your talent.

00:27:16.210 --> 00:27:18.620
I think it's the main point.

00:27:18.650 --> 00:27:20.500
And what a note to end on.

00:27:20.530 --> 00:27:21.540
Everybody nodding.

00:27:21.560 --> 00:27:23.320
Thank you ever so much,
gentlemen, for your time.

00:27:23.320 --> 00:27:24.760
It's been a real pleasure to speak to you.

00:27:24.790 --> 00:27:31.860
Some fantastic insight from some of the
best, most successful of their generation.

00:27:31.890 --> 00:27:34.980
Plenty more silverware on the cards later

00:27:35.010 --> 00:27:38.860
this season, of course,
and perhaps even later this evening.

00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:45.160
Ladies and gentlemen, Cristiano Ronaldo,
Ruben Diaz and Kyle Walker.

00:30:08.680 --> 00:30:10.140
The event is tonight.

00:30:10.170 --> 00:30:11.460
You can't be late.

00:30:11.490 --> 00:30:12.540
I will be there.

00:30:12.570 --> 00:30:15.280
I'm sending you support.

00:30:59.720 --> 00:31:00.810
We've been expecting you.

00:31:40.120 --> 00:31:42.420
So, a few clues for you.

00:31:42.450 --> 00:31:46.780
A central defensive midfielder
who is as tough as they come.

00:31:46.810 --> 00:31:49.980
A player celebrated for his
ball winning ability.

00:31:50.010 --> 00:31:52.740
Ranger passing and goal scoring.

00:31:52.770 --> 00:31:55.090
Someone who relishes the big occasion.

00:31:55.120 --> 00:31:58.900
And has shone both the club
and international level.

00:31:58.930 --> 00:32:04.680
One more clue.
He's represented his country 75 times.

00:32:04.880 --> 00:32:11.570
A player synonymous with silverware
and one of the finest the world has seen,

00:32:11.600 --> 00:32:17.420
bringing the ceremonial Globe Soccer
trophy to our breathtaking venue.

00:32:17.450 --> 00:32:19.810
A copper America champion.

00:32:19.840 --> 00:32:21.050
Have you got it yet?

00:32:21.080 --> 00:32:24.383
Well, he's also a three time La Liga winner.

00:32:26.233 --> 00:32:30.933
A five time UEFA Champions League winner

00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:36.500
and a champion of the FIFA Club World
cup three times.

00:32:36.530 --> 00:32:45.880
Ladies and gentlemen, expertly brought
in by Dubai police, the great Casemiro.

00:32:53.600 --> 00:32:55.700
Quite the entry indeed.

00:32:55.730 --> 00:32:58.460
And quite a difficult entry to follow.

00:32:58.490 --> 00:32:59.810
But we will indeed.

00:32:59.840 --> 00:33:01.780
Amanda, great to have you
back here for the awards.

00:33:01.810 --> 00:33:03.860
Oh, we will try to follow.
We will try.

00:33:03.880 --> 00:33:07.320
We welcome the world and literally
the world, tuning in from all corners

00:33:07.350 --> 00:33:11.570
of the globe with open arms to this,
the United Arab Emirates,

00:33:11.600 --> 00:33:15.117
under the leadership of
His Highness Sheik Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum,

00:33:15.217 --> 00:33:16.900
the vice president and the prime minister

00:33:16.930 --> 00:33:20.020
and the ruler of Dubai,
and under the guidance of

00:33:20.050 --> 00:33:23.220
His Highness Sheik Hamdan bin Mohammed bin
Rashid Al Maktoum,

00:33:23.250 --> 00:33:28.050
the crown prince of Dubai and the chairman
of Dubai's executive council.

00:33:28.080 --> 00:33:31.380
A huge thank you to our illustrious

00:33:31.410 --> 00:33:36.570
partners, sponsors and stakeholders
who work tirelessly to make

00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:42.960
the Nakheel Dubai Globe Soccer awards,
the spectacle that it is today.

00:33:43.840 --> 00:33:47.700
From our strategic partner,
the Dubai Sports Council,

00:33:47.730 --> 00:33:54.366
and supporting partners, Esaad,
our platinum sponsors, Audi Al Nabooda Automobiles,

00:33:54.367 --> 00:33:59.570
Emirates, Serie A,
Power Horse and Koora Break.

00:33:59.600 --> 00:34:03.090
To our gold sponsors, Silversands, Italpreziosi,

00:34:03.120 --> 00:34:12.480
Atlantis, Tatatu, Sushisamba,
Montegrappa, XDubai and Majesty Yachts.

00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:17.960
Not forgetting our Media Partners,
our event host broadcaster MBC, CNN, Marca,

00:34:21.520 --> 00:34:27.300
SSC, LaPresse, Sky, SportBusiness
and of course, IMAGO.

00:34:27.330 --> 00:34:32.500
Excitment, as you can imagine,
has been building up in our voting process.

00:34:33.890 --> 00:34:46.159
We tallied 70 million votes coming from across
over 200 territories heading into tonight's ceremony.

00:34:46.160 --> 00:34:52.580
Well, in an evening where we applaud
excellence, stars from around the world

00:34:52.610 --> 00:34:57.690
are with us at the spectacular
Atlantis The Palm.

00:34:57.720 --> 00:35:07.200
From all time greats to rising stars, all
have made their way to our iconic city.

00:35:07.414 --> 00:35:14.257
We have with us, Manchester City
and their squad of Champions, the one and only...

00:35:14.480 --> 00:35:14.960
Tom...

00:35:14.960 --> 00:35:17.170
We've got a little technical problem,
so I'm going to pick up here.

00:35:17.200 --> 00:35:21.980
Sorry.
We have with us Manchester City and their

00:35:22.010 --> 00:35:26.210
squad of champions, the one
and only Cristiano Ronaldo.

00:35:26.240 --> 00:35:28.940
Former England and Chelsea
captain, John Terry.

00:35:28.970 --> 00:35:31.780
The legend that is Fabio Capello.

00:35:31.810 --> 00:35:36.260
The Manchester United duo
of Harry Maguire and Casemiro.

00:35:36.290 --> 00:35:41.380
Super agents Jorge Mendes,
Ali Barat and Frank Trimboli,

00:35:41.410 --> 00:35:47.120
and of course, the World cup
winning coach Lionel Scaloni.

00:35:53.129 --> 00:35:59.380
2023 was a magical footballing year as

00:35:59.410 --> 00:36:06.060
footballers around the world left
an enduring mark on the beautiful game.

00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:06.460
Yeah.

00:36:06.490 --> 00:36:09.540
After a year which provided an array
of magical moments,

00:36:09.570 --> 00:36:15.380
we come together tonight to honor,
well, you, the very, very best.

00:36:15.410 --> 00:36:19.500
We are live and interactive on all social
media platforms,

00:36:19.530 --> 00:36:25.460
so don't forget
to use the hashtag #globesoccer.

00:36:25.490 --> 00:36:28.650
Listen, before we go any further,

00:36:28.680 --> 00:36:33.300
I'm sure each and every one of you in this
room will know that it has been a sad few

00:36:33.330 --> 00:36:40.500
months across the football world as we
have lost three iconic figures recently.

00:36:40.530 --> 00:36:44.130
Tonight,
we here at the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards

00:36:44.160 --> 00:36:49.260
would like to come together to pay
tributes to three legendary World Cup winners.

00:36:49.290 --> 00:36:53.900
In October last year,
former England and Manchester United icon

00:36:53.930 --> 00:37:00.420
Sir Bobby Charlton passed away
86, while at the beginning of January,

00:37:00.450 --> 00:37:04.320
just a few weeks ago,
we lost brazilian Mario Zagallo,

00:37:04.350 --> 00:37:09.620
the first man, of course, to win the
FIFA World cup as both player and coach.

00:37:09.650 --> 00:37:13.740
And then just days ago,
we lost another -

00:37:13.770 --> 00:37:17.940
German Great Franz Beckenbauer, the second man to have
won the World Cup as a player and coach.

00:37:17.970 --> 00:37:22.260
He passed away at the age of 78.

00:37:22.290 --> 00:37:26.580
Three men, three greats
who left a lasting legacy.

00:37:26.610 --> 00:37:33.440
Rest in peace, Sir Bobby Charlton,
Mario Zagallo and Franz Beckenbauer.

00:37:41.040 --> 00:37:44.210
So, on with the show.
Yeah.

00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:49.420
Without further ado,
let's get the ball rolling.

00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:51.260
So let's kick off the awards, if we may.

00:37:51.290 --> 00:37:54.690
The first award is one that recognizes

00:37:54.720 --> 00:38:00.650
the efforts of the stars on the rise,
players whose potential knows no bounds,

00:38:00.680 --> 00:38:04.940
and the player who's destined to reach
the very summit of the football world.

00:38:04.970 --> 00:38:08.460
This year, no different,
as our list of nominees for the

00:38:08.490 --> 00:38:13.860
Power Horse Emerging Player of the Year features
the finest young stars who, in fact,

00:38:13.890 --> 00:38:17.020
they've already left their
mark on the beautiful game.

00:38:17.040 --> 00:38:21.280
Your finalists for the
Power Horse Emerging Player are...

00:38:53.383 --> 00:38:56.359
So we're on to the first winner of the evening.

00:38:56.360 --> 00:39:01.580
This is the Power Horse Emerging Player at this,
the 14th Dubai Globe Soccer Awards.

00:39:01.610 --> 00:39:04.160
And the winner is

00:39:06.760 --> 00:39:11.720
England, Real Madrid,
midfielder - Jude Bellingham.

00:39:17.560 --> 00:39:20.460
Well, sadly, Jude Bellingham can't
be here with us this evening.

00:39:20.480 --> 00:39:21.860
He's in camp with Real Madrid.

00:39:21.890 --> 00:39:28.100
But the latest recipient of the Power Horse Emerging Player
award sent us this video.

00:39:28.130 --> 00:39:30.940
Hi, everyone.
I just want to thank Globe Soccer,

00:39:30.970 --> 00:39:33.060
Dubai Sports Council and of course

00:39:33.090 --> 00:39:36.170
the fans for voting me
for this brilliant award.

00:39:36.200 --> 00:39:39.460
Sorry I couldn't attend in person,
but I'm very grateful to receive it.

00:39:39.490 --> 00:39:41.360
Thank you all.

00:39:44.840 --> 00:39:48.500
Thank you, Jude, and congratulations.

00:39:48.530 --> 00:39:53.260
Now, also last year there was the crowning
of new world champions,

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:58.860
the consolidation of greatness
and the rise of emerging forces.

00:39:58.890 --> 00:40:02.740
Amongst the glory,
there emerged superstars aplenty.

00:40:02.760 --> 00:40:04.260
Looking at individual performances,

00:40:04.290 --> 00:40:08.820
team contributions and efforts across both
domestic clubs and national teams,

00:40:08.850 --> 00:40:15.580
we answer the question now of just who is
the Best Women's Footballer in the world?

00:40:15.610 --> 00:40:18.650
Indeed.
So let's move on to your finalists

00:40:18.680 --> 00:40:22.740
for the Nakheel Dubai Globe Soccer
Awards Best Women's Player.

00:40:22.770 --> 00:40:25.960
And the finalists are...

00:41:10.520 --> 00:41:12.580
All very deserving winners.

00:41:12.610 --> 00:41:17.100
But there is one who has without doubt
dominated in the last twelve months.

00:41:17.130 --> 00:41:23.120
This award has been sponsored
by Esaad and the winner is...

00:41:25.600 --> 00:41:30.520
Aitana Bonmati from Spain and FC Barcelona.

00:41:34.760 --> 00:41:39.320
So let's hear from the Best Women's Player
at the Dubai Globe Soccer awards.

00:41:39.350 --> 00:41:40.750
Here is Aitana Bonmati.

00:41:42.250 --> 00:41:44.433
Hello, I am Aitana Bonmati.

00:41:44.450 --> 00:41:50.167
I would have liked to be here in Dubai with you, but as you know, I have an important commitment with the club.

00:41:50.440 --> 00:41:56.967
We are playing the Super Cup in Madrid, so I wanted to send you a message of thanks for the award.

00:41:56.968 --> 00:42:02.083
As I always like to say, these individual awards come after a great collective effort.

00:42:02.250 --> 00:42:08.017
You also know that this year we were lucky enough to win the Champions League with Barça.

00:42:08.018 --> 00:42:11.550
The World Cup with the national team
has been a unique and round year,

00:42:11.551 --> 00:42:19.467
so I owe it all to my teammates, staff,
club workers, directors and the national team.

00:42:19.667 --> 00:42:22.367
A big hug and I wish you all the best.

00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:30.060
Well, it was only going to be a good
reason that Aitana couldn't be here.

00:42:30.080 --> 00:42:31.620
She said she would have loved to have been

00:42:31.650 --> 00:42:38.060
here in Dubai, but Barça have a game
against Madrid in the Super Cup.

00:42:38.080 --> 00:42:39.820
She said she's grateful for the award,

00:42:39.850 --> 00:42:43.280
but individual honors are
the result of teamwork, she said.

00:42:43.280 --> 00:42:45.690
There's a bit of a team there
this evening, isn't there?

00:42:45.720 --> 00:42:48.020
Aitana said she says she owes everything

00:42:48.050 --> 00:42:52.500
to her teammates, staff, managers,
as well as everyone at the national team.

00:42:52.520 --> 00:42:55.060
Yeah.
Congratulations to both of our first two

00:42:55.090 --> 00:42:59.860
winners of the evening, and thanks
again to Aitana for those kind words.

00:42:59.890 --> 00:43:02.650
We at the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards.

00:43:02.680 --> 00:43:06.940
Well, we've got a bit of an announcement
for you, a little bit of a surprise.

00:43:06.970 --> 00:43:09.900
As we mentioned, not our first rodeo,
done a few of these.

00:43:09.930 --> 00:43:12.820
But the big news is

00:43:12.850 --> 00:43:18.900
we here at the divine Globe Soccer Awards
are truly by name and by nature,

00:43:18.930 --> 00:43:22.420
going global this year,
the football world is bracing itself

00:43:22.450 --> 00:43:27.690
for the inaugural event of our
very first intercontinental series.

00:43:27.720 --> 00:43:30.170
And the first stop,

00:43:30.200 --> 00:43:31.780
any ideas?

00:43:31.810 --> 00:43:33.690
Well, I'll give you one clue.

00:43:33.720 --> 00:43:36.360
It's in Europe.

00:43:40.880 --> 00:43:44.360
After more than ten years in Dubai,

00:43:44.800 --> 00:43:48.260
the Globe Soccer awards head
to the stunning Costas Smeralda region

00:43:48.290 --> 00:43:53.160
in Sardinia for the first stop
of the intercontinental series.

00:43:53.800 --> 00:43:58.280
The inaugural european edition will be
held at the iconic Cala di Volpe Hotel

00:43:58.310 --> 00:44:06.100
in May 2024,
where the best european football talent

00:44:06.130 --> 00:44:10.480
will be rewarded for their
outstanding achievements.

00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:18.620
Sardinia, the end of May.

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:19.820
Sounds like a good idea.

00:44:19.850 --> 00:44:21.580
I'm in.

00:44:21.610 --> 00:44:22.780
Do join us there.

00:44:22.810 --> 00:44:24.980
Right on with the awards.

00:44:25.010 --> 00:44:28.383
We'd now like to welcome onto stage

00:44:28.384 --> 00:44:31.766
His Highness Sheikh Mansoor bin Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum,

00:44:31.767 --> 00:44:34.740
the Chairman of the Dubai Sports Council,

00:44:34.770 --> 00:44:37.960
accompanied by
His Excellency Mattar al Tayer,

00:44:37.990 --> 00:44:42.250
Vice Chairman of the Dubai Sports
Council, to present the awards.

00:45:05.280 --> 00:45:08.260
Welcome.
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:45:08.290 --> 00:45:10.900
Now, it has been a year where football

00:45:10.930 --> 00:45:14.140
in the Middle East has really
captured the imagination.

00:45:14.170 --> 00:45:16.420
Domestic and regional brilliance has seen

00:45:16.450 --> 00:45:20.340
plenty of focus fixed
firmly on the region.

00:45:20.370 --> 00:45:23.860
And with several big name arrivals you
might just have heard about,

00:45:23.880 --> 00:45:27.180
clubs from across the Middle East
have really embraced the spotlight.

00:45:27.210 --> 00:45:30.180
Consistency and ultimately excellence was

00:45:30.210 --> 00:45:34.020
essential in us honoring
the Best Club in the Middle East.

00:45:34.040 --> 00:45:37.140
Yeah, this one's generously
sponsored by our friends at Tatatu.

00:45:37.160 --> 00:45:39.740
Let's have a look at the finalists then,
for you in this category.

00:45:39.770 --> 00:45:42.240
And the finalists are...

00:45:59.520 --> 00:46:04.240
And your Nakheel Dubai
Globe Soccer award for Best Middle East Club goes to

00:46:08.133 --> 00:46:10.567
Egyptian Giants Al Ahly.

00:46:24.440 --> 00:46:29.820
Now, collecting the award fo Best Middle East Club of the Year
is the president of Al Ahly.

00:46:29.850 --> 00:46:34.360
Please welcome to the stage
Mahmoud el Khatib.

00:46:56.480 --> 00:46:59.800
I understand you want to say a few words.

00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:04.400
All yours.

00:49:02.080 --> 00:49:04.020
Mahmoud el Khatib,
congratulations.

00:49:04.050 --> 00:49:06.100
Thank you very much.

00:49:06.130 --> 00:49:07.380
Yes, indeed.

00:49:07.410 --> 00:49:10.180
Congratulations to Al Ahly
and all the team there now.

00:49:10.210 --> 00:49:14.020
Right, from facilitating transfers
to negotiating contracts,

00:49:14.050 --> 00:49:18.020
securing sponsorship
and of course endorsement deals.

00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:21.460
As you well know, the work of an agent is

00:49:21.490 --> 00:49:25.180
extremely rewarding,
but also incredibly taxing.

00:49:25.210 --> 00:49:27.900
Or so they say.
These are the individuals

00:49:27.930 --> 00:49:31.020
who look after every aspect
of a footballer's career.

00:49:31.050 --> 00:49:34.500
And that allows the players
to do what they need to do.

00:49:34.530 --> 00:49:37.100
Focus on the job at hand, on the pitch.
Yeah.

00:49:37.120 --> 00:49:39.820
Now, over the last twelve months,
we've seen deals which have further

00:49:39.850 --> 00:49:43.500
emphasized just how crucial
the role the agent plays.

00:49:43.530 --> 00:49:50.260
And we are here tonight to pay
tribute to those often unsung heroes.

00:49:50.290 --> 00:49:52.933
Your nominees are...

00:50:09.240 --> 00:50:12.740
So this one is brought to you by X Dubai.

00:50:12.770 --> 00:50:16.900
Time now for us to unveil to you
the 2023 Dubai Globe Soccer Award

00:50:16.930 --> 00:50:20.800
Best Agent.
And the award goes to...

00:50:21.800 --> 00:50:24.520
Jorge Mendes.

00:50:50.360 --> 00:50:53.833
Jorge Mendes and his Gestifute Agency

00:50:53.834 --> 00:50:55.700
boast only the finest talents in the world.

00:50:55.730 --> 00:50:58.500
The likes of Enzo Fernandez
and Gonçalo Ramos.

00:50:58.520 --> 00:51:01.780
Congratulations.
I understand you want to say a few words.

00:51:01.810 --> 00:51:03.860
Good evening.

00:51:03.890 --> 00:51:07.260
It's an honor to be here again.

00:51:07.290 --> 00:51:11.800
Thank you very much to Globe
Soccer for the award.

00:51:11.840 --> 00:51:14.540
I'm deeply proud.

00:51:14.570 --> 00:51:20.369
Last year was one of the best
years ever of my company - Gestifute.

00:51:20.370 --> 00:51:26.432
This year I'm going to try again
to improve as much as possible to do even better,

00:51:26.433 --> 00:51:30.140
with hard work,
ambition and passion.

00:51:30.170 --> 00:51:32.980
I would like to thanks to my wife,

00:51:33.010 --> 00:51:39.980
to all my family, my Gestifute
team and managers and players.

00:51:40.010 --> 00:51:42.780
Thank you very much and
Happy New Year for all of you.

00:51:42.810 --> 00:51:44.340
Thank you.

00:51:44.370 --> 00:51:46.680
Congratulations.

00:51:50.280 --> 00:51:51.700
Congratulations.
Okay.

00:51:51.730 --> 00:51:55.820
From the agents, we now move to the master
strategist for the next award,

00:51:55.850 --> 00:52:00.500
the individual ultimately responsible
for the football operations of any club.

00:52:00.530 --> 00:52:05.260
It's now time for us to pay
tribute to the sporting directors.

00:52:05.290 --> 00:52:08.860
Their duties may vary,
but ultimately the sporting director

00:52:08.890 --> 00:52:13.100
develops and protects the overall vision
and philosophy as well as implementing

00:52:13.130 --> 00:52:17.020
strategy required for sustainable
success at the club.

00:52:17.040 --> 00:52:18.940
The link between
the boardroom and the pitch.

00:52:18.970 --> 00:52:24.860
A large part of a club's success falls
on the sporting director.

00:52:24.880 --> 00:52:26.960
Let's have a look at your
finalists in this category.

00:52:26.990 --> 00:52:29.450
And they are...

00:52:45.880 --> 00:52:48.420
Generously sponsored by Emirates,

00:52:48.450 --> 00:52:51.820
your Nakheel Dubai Globe Soccer Awards

00:52:51.850 --> 00:53:00.880
Best Sporting Director is Cristiano Guintoli.

00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:13.700
Guintoli's crown and glory came at the end
of last season when Napoli won

00:53:13.730 --> 00:53:18.180
the Scudetto for the very first time since
1990, only the third in their history.

00:53:18.200 --> 00:53:19.860
This was due to his incredible talent

00:53:19.890 --> 00:53:24.380
acquisition, transfer, maneuvering and
collaboration with coach Luciano Spaletti.

00:53:24.410 --> 00:53:26.040
A move to Juventus followed.

00:53:26.060 --> 00:53:27.210
Given his track record,

00:53:27.240 --> 00:53:32.740
there is little doubt that success
will of course find the Bianconeri.

00:53:32.770 --> 00:53:34.460
Cristiano, congratulations.

00:53:34.490 --> 00:53:38.600
Please come and say a few words.

00:53:42.400 --> 00:53:44.360
Come on.

00:53:46.800 --> 00:53:48.800
Thank you.

00:53:49.040 --> 00:53:52.300
I am honored to be here tonight.

00:53:52.330 --> 00:53:58.940
And for me, 23 is very
important year, historical year.

00:53:58.970 --> 00:54:04.100
And we won the scudetto with Napoli.

00:54:04.130 --> 00:54:11.480
And I would like to thank
my president, Aurelio De Laurentiis,

00:54:11.640 --> 00:54:18.580
my coach, Luciano Spaletti, all players and all
people that worked with me in the past.

00:54:18.610 --> 00:54:22.660
Now, the last but not least is important.

00:54:22.690 --> 00:54:25.700
I want to thank my family

00:54:25.730 --> 00:54:34.200
and for me it's very, very important
because they help me to improve every day.

00:54:34.320 --> 00:54:38.260
Now, I started with a new adventures

00:54:38.290 --> 00:54:45.140
with Juventus and now our objective,

00:54:45.170 --> 00:54:51.180
we want to go directly in Champions League
and it's possible to win the Cup Italia.

00:54:51.210 --> 00:54:54.340
But in the future, I think it's important

00:54:54.370 --> 00:55:00.300
to be here again
for another award for Juventus.

00:55:00.330 --> 00:55:02.480
Thank you again.

00:55:06.280 --> 00:55:07.960
Well done indeed
to Cristiano.

00:55:07.990 --> 00:55:10.740
Well done to all the team.
Moving on to the next award.

00:55:10.770 --> 00:55:14.140
Often the difference
between success and failure.

00:55:14.170 --> 00:55:19.210
Not only does the modern day goalkeeper
have to be dominant in stopping opposition

00:55:19.240 --> 00:55:22.880
attacks, but also well capable
of initiating offensive moves as well.

00:55:22.910 --> 00:55:26.820
From sweeper, keeper, supreme stopper,
the ball playing minder.

00:55:26.850 --> 00:55:29.040
There were some blinding performances

00:55:29.070 --> 00:55:31.940
that left the football
world watching on in awe.

00:55:31.970 --> 00:55:36.860
That's why we now pay tribute
to the Best Goalkeeper.

00:55:36.890 --> 00:55:38.960
Brought to you by Sushisamba,

00:55:38.990 --> 00:55:42.400
your finalists for Best Goalkeeper are...

00:56:02.120 --> 00:56:03.820
Right then, the winner,

00:56:03.850 --> 00:56:15.040
Best Goalkeeper for the 14th annual
Dubai Globe Soccer Awards is Ederson.

00:56:20.880 --> 00:56:24.480
A shot stopper
of the highest quality!

00:56:24.960 --> 00:56:26.600
Ederson played a heroic role

00:56:26.630 --> 00:56:31.620
in Manchester City's all conquering team,
keeping 19 clean sheets in the process.

00:56:31.640 --> 00:56:33.480
With his ball playing abilities setting

00:56:33.510 --> 00:56:36.500
him apart, even claiming an assist
in the Premier League,

00:56:36.530 --> 00:56:43.440
Ederson continues to perfect the role of
sweeper, keeper and traditional stopper.

00:56:44.760 --> 00:56:46.540
The brazilian international has firmly

00:56:46.570 --> 00:56:51.760
established himself as one
of the best in the world.

00:57:18.960 --> 00:57:21.820
A quick photo first and then, of course,

00:57:21.850 --> 00:57:25.740
we'll ask Ederson for a few words.
Amanda, over to you.

00:57:25.770 --> 00:57:27.020
Congratulations.

00:57:27.050 --> 00:57:29.580
I think it was a popular choice

00:57:29.600 --> 00:57:33.540
in the room, we were talking earlier about
the fact that you said the key to this

00:57:33.570 --> 00:57:38.820
City success is that Pep
is always ten steps ahead.

00:57:38.850 --> 00:57:42.340
How tough is that for you as players?

00:57:42.370 --> 00:57:44.020
For me, it's so easy to

00:57:44.050 --> 00:57:45.100
work with Pep.

00:57:45.130 --> 00:57:49.260
I work with Pep, for like six years a half.

00:57:49.290 --> 00:57:51.580
I collected some trophies.

00:57:51.610 --> 00:57:52.860
It's very important.

00:57:52.890 --> 00:57:57.180
I think Pep is very intensive guy,
push the team open.

00:57:57.210 --> 00:58:00.940
Push the players for me is no different.

00:58:00.970 --> 00:58:02.700
Congratulations.

00:58:02.730 --> 00:58:05.140
I suspect there might be a little bit more

00:58:05.170 --> 00:58:09.260
silverware, goldware heading your
way in the not too distant future.

00:58:09.290 --> 00:58:11.980
Ederson, the Best Goalkeeper of the Year.

00:58:12.010 --> 00:58:13.880
Congratulations.

00:58:14.960 --> 00:58:17.420
Yeah, congratulations to Ederson.

00:58:17.450 --> 00:58:20.100
Yet another award for Manchester City.

00:58:20.130 --> 00:58:21.880
Okay, from goalkeeper,

00:58:21.910 --> 00:58:25.380
let's move our way up the field,
if we can the driving force,

00:58:25.410 --> 00:58:30.420
the visionaries, they're quite simply,
well, the conductors of the orchestras.

00:58:30.450 --> 00:58:32.300
We're talking midfielders here.

00:58:32.330 --> 00:58:34.260
The link between defense and attack.

00:58:34.290 --> 00:58:41.660
The midfielder needs to always be one step
ahead and often the success of a midfielder

00:58:41.690 --> 00:58:44.740
often determines the success
of the team as a whole.

00:58:44.760 --> 00:58:45.020
Yeah.

00:58:45.050 --> 00:58:48.500
As football continues to evolve,
so does the role of the midfielder

00:58:48.530 --> 00:58:54.880
and in 2023 there were some
serious players who raised the bar.

00:58:55.200 --> 00:58:58.660
Your finalists then for the
Nakheel Dubai Globe Soccer Award,

00:58:58.690 --> 00:59:01.717
Best Midfielder are...

00:59:27.040 --> 00:59:29.040
The award's been generously sponsored

00:59:29.070 --> 00:59:33.520
by Power Horse and
the Best Midfielder goes to...

00:59:36.880 --> 00:59:40.560
Manchester City's Rodri

00:59:46.600 --> 00:59:51.960
Rodri is a player who lives for the big moments.
The spaniard cemented himself as one

00:59:51.970 --> 00:59:55.420
of the finest central defensive
midfielders in the world thanks to his

00:59:55.450 --> 01:00:00.900
unwavering consistency and reliability
at the heart of midfield,

01:00:00.930 --> 01:00:04.260
with his superb shooting ability
and innate elegance,

01:00:04.290 --> 01:00:07.917
Rodri was ever present throughout City's
historic season.

01:00:08.200 --> 01:00:11.680
When it mattered the most,
he was also a match winner as he scored

01:00:11.710 --> 01:00:17.640
the goal which secured City a first
ever Champions League crown.

01:00:38.280 --> 01:00:43.860
Congratulations again to Rodri
and let's hear from him now.

01:00:43.890 --> 01:00:45.620
Just a quick word if I may.

01:00:45.650 --> 01:00:49.980
There were so many important moments,
particularly from you last season.

01:00:50.010 --> 01:00:52.500
Perhaps none more so than that goal

01:00:52.520 --> 01:00:54.860
in the Champions League
final in Istanbul, though.

01:00:54.890 --> 01:00:59.860
At what point did you allow yourself
to believe it was the winning goal?

01:00:59.890 --> 01:01:05.020
Well, I mean, to be fair,
I think it was like 20 minutes left.

01:01:05.050 --> 01:01:11.340
I didn't thought it was done,
but the gap was open.

01:01:11.370 --> 01:01:13.580
Of course we were close to it,

01:01:13.600 --> 01:01:16.900
but I remember that moment when we all
come each other and hug each other.

01:01:16.930 --> 01:01:19.820
I was saying, guys, we have
the 20 minutes of your lives.

01:01:19.850 --> 01:01:21.340
Let's keep pushing.

01:01:21.370 --> 01:01:24.340
And you can see in the chances that Eddie

01:01:24.370 --> 01:01:31.100
saves in the line and Ruben flicked to
the corner like the game wasn't finished.

01:01:31.130 --> 01:01:35.580
But when they whistle, I mean,
all the motions come into all these years

01:01:35.610 --> 01:01:40.140
that we work in the project
at the end came succeed.

01:01:40.170 --> 01:01:44.780
And I cannot be more proud
of myself and my teammates.

01:01:44.810 --> 01:01:47.180
I think was unbelievable season for us.

01:01:47.210 --> 01:01:50.060
How many times have you watched it back?

01:01:50.090 --> 01:01:52.500
I say before, I think it's of course,

01:01:52.530 --> 01:01:56.140
so far the most important
moment of my career.

01:01:56.170 --> 01:02:00.380
Maybe 5000 times,
but always it's not enough.

01:02:00.410 --> 01:02:02.500
So, yeah, very proud of what I did.

01:02:02.530 --> 01:02:07.500
My family, everyone
surrounding me is so proud.

01:02:07.530 --> 01:02:11.580
So I can only dream about doing it again.

01:02:11.600 --> 01:02:15.320
Yeah, I haven't got the math quick enough
to work out how many times that is a day.

01:02:15.320 --> 01:02:16.720
We're only, what, six months on.

01:02:16.750 --> 01:02:21.380
But congratulations, I've no doubt there's
many more really special moments to come.

01:02:21.400 --> 01:02:22.980
Thank you ever so much and well done.

01:02:23.010 --> 01:02:26.360
Please go and rejoin your teammates.

01:02:29.400 --> 01:02:31.420
Congratulations indeed.

01:02:31.450 --> 01:02:34.500
Okay, let's move to the women's game.

01:02:34.530 --> 01:02:39.940
Women's club football continues to reach
new frontiers with every passing season.

01:02:39.970 --> 01:02:42.780
2023, the standard was raised yet again.

01:02:42.810 --> 01:02:45.500
More investment gave more success,

01:02:45.530 --> 01:02:49.500
which led to clubs across the world
reaching unparalleled heights.

01:02:49.530 --> 01:02:52.540
We had league honors,
cup success, continental glory.

01:02:52.570 --> 01:02:57.180
We are here tonight in Dubai
to pay tribute to the very best.

01:02:57.210 --> 01:02:59.540
Kindly sponsored by Koora Break,

01:02:59.570 --> 01:03:02.620
your finalists
for the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards

01:03:02.650 --> 01:03:05.717
Best Women's Club are...

01:03:26.080 --> 01:03:36.280
The Best Women's Club at the
Dubai Globe Soccer Awards is FC Barcelona.

01:03:42.400 --> 01:03:45.740
It's been another dominant
year for FC Barcelona.

01:03:45.770 --> 01:03:50.780
They landed their 8th Liga F title
at a canter, winning 28 of 30 games,

01:03:50.810 --> 01:03:54.300
scoring 118 goals
and conceding just ten times.

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:56.420
This was their fourth title in a row.

01:03:56.450 --> 01:03:58.200
Having exemplified their domestic

01:03:58.200 --> 01:04:01.300
dominance, they have a score
to settle in the Champions League.

01:04:01.320 --> 01:04:03.300
Recovering from a two goal deficit against

01:04:03.330 --> 01:04:06.500
Wolfsburg in the final,
they showed their determination.

01:04:06.530 --> 01:04:08.540
The 3-2 victory ensured the trophy

01:04:08.570 --> 01:04:14.360
headed back to Catalonia
for a second time in three seasons.

01:04:19.440 --> 01:04:21.180
Accepting the award is Xavier Puig,

01:04:21.210 --> 01:04:27.240
the Director responsible for
Women’s Football at FC Barcelona.

01:04:42.960 --> 01:04:44.260
Congratulations.

01:04:44.290 --> 01:04:48.040
Please, the mic is yours.

01:04:59.200 --> 01:05:02.700
Good evening everyone.

01:05:02.730 --> 01:05:09.580
It is a pleasure for me to represent
FC Barcelona in the occasion of receiving

01:05:09.610 --> 01:05:15.260
the Best Women's Team of the Year
award at the Globe Soccer Awards.

01:05:15.290 --> 01:05:18.700
This award, the result of many people

01:05:18.730 --> 01:05:24.500
work and the club commitment
to women's football.

01:05:24.530 --> 01:05:30.140
On behalf of your player, Aitana Bonmati,

01:05:30.170 --> 01:05:36.460
I also want to thank Globe Soccer
Awards for the Best Player award.

01:05:36.490 --> 01:05:44.580
Aitana is currently in Madrid focusing
on the Super Cup final that they'll play

01:05:44.610 --> 01:05:51.180
tomorrow and we hope will be
our first trophy this season.

01:05:51.210 --> 01:05:55.180
Thank you again for these awards.

01:05:55.210 --> 01:05:56.980
We are immensely grateful.

01:05:57.010 --> 01:05:58.700
Thank you very much.

01:05:58.730 --> 01:05:59.940
Congratulations.

01:05:59.970 --> 01:06:01.920
Thank you.

01:06:03.200 --> 01:06:06.580
Congratulations to all
the team at FC Barcelona.

01:06:06.610 --> 01:06:11.740
All right, I think we should take
a moment now to honor a couple of careers.

01:06:11.770 --> 01:06:15.620
It's a nice tradition
of the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards when we

01:06:15.650 --> 01:06:19.300
get the opportunity to say thank you
to some of the greats of the game.

01:06:19.330 --> 01:06:21.300
The Career Award serves as recognition

01:06:21.330 --> 01:06:25.380
to those who have scaled the very
highest peaks of the footballing world.

01:06:25.400 --> 01:06:27.020
Players out there who've captured

01:06:27.050 --> 01:06:33.340
the imagination and who provided moments
of sheer genius on the field of play.

01:06:33.370 --> 01:06:36.660
Our first Career Award has been generously

01:06:36.690 --> 01:06:44.380
sponsored by Serie A and it goes to former

01:06:44.410 --> 01:06:48.920
England and Chelsea captain John Terry.

01:06:55.160 --> 01:06:56.740
Cheers, JT.
Well done.

01:06:56.770 --> 01:06:58.440
Cheers.

01:07:07.400 --> 01:07:08.500
Congratulations to John.

01:07:08.530 --> 01:07:10.380
Let's see if we can get a few words.

01:07:10.410 --> 01:07:12.800
Come on over.

01:07:18.040 --> 01:07:19.660
Good evening, everyone.

01:07:19.690 --> 01:07:22.380
It's a huge honor for me
to win this award tonight.

01:07:22.410 --> 01:07:25.340
I'd like to thank Dubai Sports Council

01:07:25.370 --> 01:07:28.700
and Globe Soccer Awards
for hosting us all this evening.

01:07:28.730 --> 01:07:31.180
Individual awards are fantastic to win

01:07:31.210 --> 01:07:34.460
but impossible to do without
teammates and managers.

01:07:34.480 --> 01:07:36.240
I've been very fortunate to play with some

01:07:36.270 --> 01:07:39.900
great managers and some of the best
players across the world as well.

01:07:39.920 --> 01:07:41.700
I'd like to dedicate this award this

01:07:41.730 --> 01:07:45.500
evening to a man that gave
me my debut a long time ago,

01:07:45.530 --> 01:07:50.720
Gianluca Vialli, who sadly
lost his life last year.

01:07:56.680 --> 01:07:59.000
Luca was a manager that believed in me

01:07:59.000 --> 01:08:01.980
and gave me my first opportunity
at Chelsea and I'm very thankful for that.

01:08:02.010 --> 01:08:04.020
So, Luca, this one's for you.

01:08:04.050 --> 01:08:07.480
I love you and thank you.

01:08:09.240 --> 01:08:16.620
Just before you go,
if there was one thing that Luca Vialli

01:08:16.640 --> 01:08:20.780
taught you, told you that you
carry with you, what would it be?

01:08:20.800 --> 01:08:22.720
He said to me, I'll never forget it.

01:08:22.750 --> 01:08:24.540
He said to me in the showers,

01:08:24.570 --> 01:08:28.580
don't do what I do, do what I say,
and that stays with me.

01:08:28.600 --> 01:08:32.060
I'm just checking,
have you got your kids under there?

01:08:32.090 --> 01:08:34.560
I have, actually.

01:08:35.520 --> 01:08:41.300
And listen, Chelsea, at the moment
it's not been the best run for them.

01:08:41.330 --> 01:08:46.140
There was a call this week that perhaps
you should get in that dressing room.

01:08:46.170 --> 01:08:50.260
If you were in that dressing room,
what would your message be?

01:08:50.280 --> 01:08:52.340
You know what, I think
we're seeing cycles.

01:08:52.370 --> 01:08:54.660
I think when I look back 10-15 years ago,

01:08:54.680 --> 01:08:56.740
Man United were dominating
the Premier League.

01:08:56.760 --> 01:08:57.540
Chelsea came along,

01:08:57.570 --> 01:09:01.500
we dominated for a little bit and now
Pep and Man City are dominating.

01:09:01.530 --> 01:09:04.580
And I've said it for a little bit now.

01:09:04.600 --> 01:09:06.180
It's going to be hard to catch them.

01:09:06.200 --> 01:09:08.980
They're the best team,
they've got some great individual players

01:09:09.000 --> 01:09:11.900
and the way they do it year
after year is incredible.

01:09:11.920 --> 01:09:14.180
I managed to win the Premier League twice

01:09:14.210 --> 01:09:16.660
on the bounce and it's
very difficult to do so.

01:09:16.680 --> 01:09:18.700
I wish them well.
They're a fantastic team.

01:09:18.720 --> 01:09:21.340
But unfortunately, Chelsea are
a little bit off it at the moment.

01:09:21.360 --> 01:09:23.260
But given time, the manager needs time.

01:09:23.290 --> 01:09:24.880
Pochettino is a great manager.

01:09:24.910 --> 01:09:26.980
I've seen him work on a daily basis.

01:09:27.000 --> 01:09:28.680
We're a young squad of players as well,

01:09:28.710 --> 01:09:32.900
but we're a long way off of the likes
of Man City and Liverpool at the moment.

01:09:32.920 --> 01:09:34.860
Congratulations.
Enjoy this moment.

01:09:34.880 --> 01:09:35.620
Thank you.
Well done.

01:09:35.640 --> 01:09:37.700
Thank you, everyone.

01:09:37.720 --> 01:09:39.540
Congratulations to John.

01:09:39.570 --> 01:09:41.180
Well deserved.

01:09:41.210 --> 01:09:47.300
Right, enjoy now, as we get into the next
of our awards, time now to pay tribute

01:09:47.330 --> 01:09:52.740
to yet another star who's secured his
place in the history books of the game.

01:09:52.760 --> 01:09:56.220
This award is brought
to you by Silversands.

01:09:56.250 --> 01:10:00.460
Ladies and gentlemen,
our next Career Award winner is none other than

01:10:04.883 --> 01:10:09.640
World Cup winning
coach Lionel Scaloni.

01:10:12.160 --> 01:10:16.780
Lionel Scaloni was the architect of one
of football's most fascinating stories.

01:10:16.800 --> 01:10:22.420
Taking over a struggling Argentina team in
2018, he helped them find a new identity.

01:10:22.450 --> 01:10:24.540
Los Albiceleste flourished.

01:10:24.570 --> 01:10:28.940
Success of the Cup America
in 2021 ended a 28 year drought.

01:10:28.960 --> 01:10:30.780
But the best was yet to come.

01:10:30.800 --> 01:10:32.620
With Leo Messi at the forefront,

01:10:32.640 --> 01:10:36.540
Argentina felt as if they had
a date with destiny in Qatar.

01:10:36.570 --> 01:10:38.300
After a final for the ages,

01:10:38.330 --> 01:10:41.860
Argentina were world champions
for a third time in their history.

01:10:41.880 --> 01:10:46.840
Scaloni has catapulted into greatness.

01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:09.460
So many congratulations.

01:11:09.490 --> 01:11:12.760
The mic is yours.

01:11:14.360 --> 01:11:16.700
Hello.
Sorry for my English.

01:11:16.720 --> 01:11:18.700
It's very bad.

01:11:18.720 --> 01:11:22.120
I speak Spanish.

01:11:22.200 --> 01:11:25.600
Thank you very much for the award.

01:11:25.643 --> 01:11:29.400
I dedicate it to my country, to my people.

01:11:33.080 --> 01:11:37.843
Sincerely, it has been a movie,
a film, what we have achieved.

01:11:38.671 --> 01:11:43.486
I dedicate it to them, to all Argentines,
to my technical staff,

01:11:43.571 --> 01:11:54.528
to Pablo Aimar, to Walter Samuel, Roberto Ayala,
Matías Manna, Martin Tocalli, Luis Martín, Rodrigo Barrios

01:11:54.529 --> 01:12:00.543
all of them who have helped me to get this incredible award.

01:12:00.743 --> 01:12:05.243
To my family, who is here today,
my wife and my children, I love you.

01:12:05.244 --> 01:12:09.257
Thank you very much.
That's all I have to say. Thank you.

01:12:12.200 --> 01:12:15.640
So many congratulations.

01:12:17.480 --> 01:12:20.980
I don't think we got the answer
to whether or not you've persuaded

01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:25.020
Leo Messi to stick around for 2026 or not.
Tom.

01:12:25.040 --> 01:12:27.020
We move on,
then to the next of our awards.

01:12:27.040 --> 01:12:28.220
Thank you very much
indeed for your patience.

01:12:28.240 --> 01:12:29.500
All those tuning in around the world,

01:12:29.530 --> 01:12:33.900
all of us with us here in Dubai
tonight on this evening of winners.

01:12:33.920 --> 01:12:36.340
Next up, the quest to be recognized as,

01:12:36.370 --> 01:12:38.500
quite simply,
the finest club in the world.

01:12:38.530 --> 01:12:39.660
It's never ending.

01:12:39.680 --> 01:12:41.840
Find the perfect balance, both on and off

01:12:41.870 --> 01:12:45.540
the pitch is where the good
gets separated from the great.

01:12:45.570 --> 01:12:48.900
In 2023, bar was raised.

01:12:48.920 --> 01:12:52.540
And in an era when football has been
at this most competitive,

01:12:52.570 --> 01:12:57.700
there were clubs out there who flourished,
which allowed them to excel yet further.

01:12:57.720 --> 01:13:00.520
Your nominees for the
Best Men's Club are...

01:13:40.320 --> 01:13:42.780
For the Best Men's Club,

01:13:42.800 --> 01:13:47.060
this year's Nakheel Dubai Globe
Soccer awards are...

01:13:47.090 --> 01:13:49.860
Time for something
a little bit special, I think.

01:13:49.880 --> 01:13:51.260
The team who won

01:13:51.290 --> 01:13:58.560
the Premier League for a 7th time
and 5th in the last six seasons.

01:14:04.320 --> 01:14:11.960
The club who also lifted the FA Cup
for the 7th time in their history.

01:14:19.400 --> 01:14:25.640
The undefeated winners
of the UEFA Champions League.

01:14:34.840 --> 01:14:35.540
Which, of course,

01:14:35.570 --> 01:14:40.920
allowed them to go on to win the
UEFA Super cup for the very first time.

01:14:51.160 --> 01:14:58.720
And the team who landed the FIFA Club
World cup on their tournament debut.

01:15:03.960 --> 01:15:06.620
So, any ideas?

01:15:06.640 --> 01:15:14.920
Well, the Best Men's Club are
none other than Manchester City.

01:15:26.240 --> 01:15:31.160
Their status as the Premier League's
finest has long been established.

01:15:31.320 --> 01:15:35.220
Global success is what
Manchester City crave the most.

01:15:35.250 --> 01:15:37.220
Victory over Inter Milan, City landed

01:15:37.250 --> 01:15:40.580
the UEFA Champions League
title for the very first time.

01:15:40.610 --> 01:15:44.100
A culmination of years of hard work.

01:15:44.130 --> 01:15:47.940
Victory over Fluminense,
the final piece of the puzzle was placed.

01:15:47.960 --> 01:15:50.460
The city won the FIFA Club World cup,

01:15:50.490 --> 01:15:54.100
in the process becoming the first english
club to simultaneously hold

01:15:54.130 --> 01:15:57.660
the Premier League, FA Cup,
UEFA Champions League,

01:15:57.680 --> 01:16:05.600
UEFA Super Cup and the FIFA Club World
Cup, securing City sporting immortality.

01:16:14.320 --> 01:16:15.860
What a season.

01:16:15.880 --> 01:16:17.620
What a trophy hall.

01:16:17.640 --> 01:16:22.340
Manchester City deservedly
named Best Men's Club.

01:16:22.370 --> 01:16:24.580
Going to ask the rest of the team to come

01:16:24.610 --> 01:16:28.940
up and join us on stage
with your teammates.

01:16:28.960 --> 01:16:32.580
And Kevin, please come on over.

01:16:32.610 --> 01:16:38.760
Maybe you could hand off that trophy
to one of your teammates.

01:16:41.160 --> 01:16:44.140
Kevin, come and get your
hands on another trophy.

01:16:44.170 --> 01:16:45.960
Just here.

01:16:53.680 --> 01:16:54.940
Come on in, everyone.

01:16:54.960 --> 01:16:57.120
Come on in.

01:17:00.720 --> 01:17:02.020
Come on.
Come on in.

01:17:02.040 --> 01:17:03.100
Round for the team pic.

01:17:03.130 --> 01:17:06.180
Everybody huddle in.

01:17:06.210 --> 01:17:07.500
Huddle in.

01:17:07.530 --> 01:17:10.820
Let's hear it one for the
Team of the Year.

01:17:10.840 --> 01:17:13.240
Manchester City.

01:17:23.560 --> 01:17:26.420
So, Kevin, we touched on it a little bit

01:17:26.450 --> 01:17:30.900
earlier, but this was the big one,
wasn't it, for Manchester City.

01:17:30.920 --> 01:17:34.700
Getting your hands on the
Champions League at last.

01:17:34.720 --> 01:17:38.000
What has that meant for you personally?

01:17:38.080 --> 01:17:41.340
Well, it's the one that I
missed with this team.

01:17:41.370 --> 01:17:47.660
I've been here for nine years and it's
been a lot of heartache

01:17:47.680 --> 01:17:53.020
going through the Champions League,
but last year was amazing.

01:17:53.050 --> 01:17:57.940
And, yeah, these guys helped me win this
trophy, so I'm very grateful to everybody

01:17:57.960 --> 01:18:02.460
for the club, for the guys,
and at least I got one.

01:18:02.490 --> 01:18:03.460
And going on,

01:18:03.480 --> 01:18:05.080
what are you thinking
in terms of this year?

01:18:05.110 --> 01:18:09.900
I mean, it's looking pretty good so
far in terms of repeating the success.

01:18:09.920 --> 01:18:12.980
Well, I've seen these
guys play all season.

01:18:13.000 --> 01:18:19.360
I've just been sitting on the sidelines
and these guys are amazing.

01:18:19.880 --> 01:18:21.720
They did really well in all

01:18:21.750 --> 01:18:25.380
the competitions and this
team is ready to go again.

01:18:25.410 --> 01:18:29.500
I see the hunger, see the passion,
and let's try again.

01:18:29.530 --> 01:18:34.500
Sitting on the sidelines and, if reports
are to be believed, working on your hair.

01:18:34.530 --> 01:18:36.900
What's the secret to that?

01:18:36.920 --> 01:18:40.760
Just don't go to the barber.

01:18:41.040 --> 01:18:42.500
Congratulations.

01:18:42.530 --> 01:18:46.780
We look forward to seeing how it grows
and develops, much like the trophy win.

01:18:46.800 --> 01:18:49.340
Manchester City.
Congratulations, Manchester City.

01:18:49.370 --> 01:18:51.920
And Kevin de Bruyne.

01:18:55.320 --> 01:18:59.740
Yeah, congratulations to the entire team
and a huge thanks to all the team

01:18:59.760 --> 01:19:03.500
from Manchester City for being
with us here tonight.

01:19:03.530 --> 01:19:06.300
So we turn our attention then to the next

01:19:06.330 --> 01:19:11.460
of our awards as we come very close
towards the conclusion of proceedings.

01:19:11.490 --> 01:19:15.820
Still some big awards to be handed out
from the world champions and continental

01:19:15.840 --> 01:19:19.220
champions, and players with trophy
cabinets brimming with accolades.

01:19:19.250 --> 01:19:25.500
There's been a steady influx of global
superstars right here in the Middle East.

01:19:25.530 --> 01:19:29.420
Add to that a plethora of homegrown talent

01:19:29.450 --> 01:19:33.660
and football in the Middle
East is at its most formidable.

01:19:33.680 --> 01:19:37.100
That's been evident in some brilliant
performances over the last year.

01:19:37.130 --> 01:19:43.060
But who has been the player who delivered
the very best and most consistently?

01:19:43.090 --> 01:19:47.340
Yeah, this one's kindly sponsored
by our friends at Italipreziosi.

01:19:47.370 --> 01:19:50.840
And the finalists then, are...

01:20:11.920 --> 01:20:13.620
Ladies and gentlemen,

01:20:13.640 --> 01:20:19.580
the winner of the Dubai Globe Soccer
Awards Best Middle East Player...

01:20:19.610 --> 01:20:29.240
I think the roof is about to go off..
Is none other than Cristiano Ronaldo.

01:20:32.600 --> 01:20:37.860
It was a magical year for you, Cristiano,
and the accolades just keep on coming.

01:20:37.880 --> 01:20:42.060
Your 54 goals in 2023 impressively also

01:20:42.090 --> 01:20:46.540
secures you the Maradona Award,
brought to you by Nakheel.

01:20:46.570 --> 01:20:50.580
Extraordinarily, this trophy actually

01:20:50.610 --> 01:20:58.720
has the exact replica of the late,
great Diego Maradona's foot.

01:20:59.520 --> 01:21:01.680
Cristiano Ronaldo further added to his

01:21:01.710 --> 01:21:05.540
legacy by taking his talents
to Al-Nassr in Saudi Arabia.

01:21:05.560 --> 01:21:07.360
His foresight made the globalization

01:21:07.380 --> 01:21:12.060
of football a reality as the eyes of the
world shifted towards the Middle East.

01:21:12.090 --> 01:21:13.980
Ronaldo's prowess on the pitch is

01:21:14.000 --> 01:21:16.620
undeniable,
but it's his ability for making

01:21:16.640 --> 01:21:20.140
revolutionary decisions off
it which sets him apart.

01:21:20.170 --> 01:21:24.860
Now, in Riyadh, and spear in the attack
for Al-Nassr, they become the team to beat.

01:21:24.880 --> 01:21:31.540
The year 2023 ended with CR7 netting
a staggering and world leading 54 goals.

01:21:31.570 --> 01:21:36.600
Both for Al-Nassr and the
Portuguese National team.

01:21:53.680 --> 01:21:55.740
Another Globe Soccer Award for Cristiano.

01:21:55.760 --> 01:21:57.060
Let's get a few words with them.

01:21:57.090 --> 01:21:59.620
Cristiano, congratulations.

01:21:59.640 --> 01:22:01.740
Cristiano, we were talking earlier about

01:22:01.760 --> 01:22:04.420
how you used the motivation
of some of the criticism.

01:22:04.450 --> 01:22:09.560
How important was that first goal
that you scored in Saudi Arabia?

01:22:09.560 --> 01:22:12.700
Do you remember?
It was a penalty, I think.

01:22:12.720 --> 01:22:14.700
Yes, I remember.
It was a good moment.

01:22:14.720 --> 01:22:17.040
It was my first one.

01:22:17.640 --> 01:22:18.440
It was good.

01:22:18.460 --> 01:22:24.740
It wasn't special because the first
one is always special, but it was good.

01:22:24.760 --> 01:22:25.980
I was so proud.

01:22:26.000 --> 01:22:29.760
I did amazing season.

01:22:30.840 --> 01:22:33.700
I have to say thank you to my teammates,

01:22:33.720 --> 01:22:41.540
my coaches from Al-Nassr, from Portugal
national team, and I feel so proud.

01:22:41.570 --> 01:22:42.900
I never won this trophy.

01:22:42.920 --> 01:22:46.140
The Best Middle East player
and Maradona Award as well.

01:22:46.170 --> 01:22:49.180
So I will put

01:22:49.210 --> 01:22:55.220
with passion in my museum because it's
two special ones and I'm so proud.

01:22:55.250 --> 01:23:01.460
I have to say thank you to my wife,
to my kids that deal with me every day.

01:23:01.480 --> 01:23:03.460
Sometimes I know I'm a little bit boring,

01:23:03.490 --> 01:23:08.020
but it's my job to be
consistent every time.

01:23:08.050 --> 01:23:14.180
So thank you to the Globe Soccer
for this amazing award.

01:23:14.210 --> 01:23:17.740
And you have said this is
about more than just you.

01:23:17.760 --> 01:23:21.860
This is about growing football
in the game in another region.

01:23:21.880 --> 01:23:26.860
How confident are you that the influx
of players will continue?

01:23:26.880 --> 01:23:28.180
I hope so.

01:23:28.210 --> 01:23:34.060
As I say before
the league, the leagues start

01:23:34.090 --> 01:23:39.940
one year ago to grow and grow,
and I'm sure 100% they will continue

01:23:39.960 --> 01:23:46.260
to grow because our boss,
they decide and they love football.

01:23:46.290 --> 01:23:49.420
And in my opinion, the league will be top.

01:23:49.450 --> 01:23:50.780
Top.

01:23:50.800 --> 01:23:52.340
Well, top, top.

01:23:52.360 --> 01:23:54.020
You've got another trophy to collect.

01:23:54.040 --> 01:23:56.820
If I can just usher you back over there.
This is a pretty special,

01:23:56.840 --> 01:24:00.140
the Maradona award, complete
with a replica of the foot.

01:24:00.170 --> 01:24:02.320
Congratulations.

01:24:09.960 --> 01:24:12.060
Yeah, congratulations to Cristiano.

01:24:12.090 --> 01:24:14.540
He's going to need all his hands there

01:24:14.570 --> 01:24:20.220
for the two trophies as well as
he makes his way off the stage.

01:24:20.250 --> 01:24:23.740
Right from one tactical genius to another,

01:24:23.760 --> 01:24:26.100
the tactical genius is
the master motivator.

01:24:26.130 --> 01:24:28.620
Strategic excellence may be a fundamental

01:24:28.640 --> 01:24:31.420
factor, but leadership,
communication and the ability to bring

01:24:31.450 --> 01:24:35.980
the best out of any player means
success is almost a certainty.

01:24:36.000 --> 01:24:40.180
In 2023, there were coaches,
coaches whose legacies were enhanced.

01:24:40.210 --> 01:24:40.940
And we here

01:24:40.960 --> 01:24:47.700
at the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards boast
an esteemed list of Best Coach nominees.

01:24:47.720 --> 01:24:51.000
Your finalists for the
Best Coach of the Year are...

01:25:29.320 --> 01:25:37.960
The best coach of the year at the
Globe Soccer Awards is Pep Guardiola.

01:25:43.240 --> 01:25:47.380
With fundamentals surrounding possession,
pressing creativity,

01:25:47.410 --> 01:25:52.880
Pep Guardiola has been at the forefront
of the beautiful game's evolution.

01:25:53.760 --> 01:25:56.100
Having stamped his authority in Barcelona

01:25:56.130 --> 01:26:02.080
and Munich, Guardiola's status was
further elevated at Manchester City.

01:26:04.160 --> 01:26:05.740
After dominating the Premier League,

01:26:05.760 --> 01:26:09.900
he secured european,
then global success in 2023,

01:26:09.920 --> 01:26:14.900
the Champions League in June,
followed by the Club World Cup triumph.

01:26:14.920 --> 01:26:19.080
This is a coach who has an obsessive eye
for detail, with the ability to get

01:26:19.110 --> 01:26:22.300
the very best out of every
player he's worked with.

01:26:22.330 --> 01:26:25.220
2023 is a special year for a

01:26:25.250 --> 01:26:28.040
Special Coach.

01:26:55.280 --> 01:26:56.420
Congratulations.

01:26:56.450 --> 01:26:59.480
I'll just bring you back this little bit.

01:27:00.640 --> 01:27:01.900
Firstly, happy birthday.

01:27:01.920 --> 01:27:05.820
Not a bad birthday celebration,
getting your hands on another trophy.

01:27:05.840 --> 01:27:09.140
But what does it feel like
being the best in the world?

01:27:09.170 --> 01:27:11.800
Because we won.

01:27:12.520 --> 01:27:14.980
If we don't win, we are not even invited.

01:27:16.100 --> 01:27:18.460
So that is the truth.

01:27:18.490 --> 01:27:21.140
So to win, there are many, many reasons.

01:27:21.170 --> 01:27:23.980
So especially all of them
are sitting there.

01:27:24.000 --> 01:27:31.060
And of course, we are here in UAE,
where Abu Dhabi held unconditionally.

01:27:31.090 --> 01:27:33.180
Yeah, really, really happy.

01:27:33.210 --> 01:27:37.420
How much do you allow yourself
to celebrate the successes?

01:27:37.450 --> 01:27:39.280
A lot.

01:27:39.360 --> 01:27:42.420
But it's on to next as quick as possible.

01:27:42.440 --> 01:27:43.740
But of course we celebrate it.

01:27:43.770 --> 01:27:46.140
And especially when the days come through,

01:27:46.160 --> 01:27:49.860
the years come through, you'll remember
there will be no forgotten for all of us.

01:27:49.880 --> 01:27:50.860
That's for sure.

01:27:50.880 --> 01:27:53.180
And have you managed to come
up with an answer yet?

01:27:53.200 --> 01:27:56.660
Which is the best?
Your Barcelona team or this one?

01:27:56.690 --> 01:28:00.100
It's like as mom and dad to choose.

01:28:00.130 --> 01:28:02.820
Both are special.
Which is which?

01:28:02.840 --> 01:28:04.380
I'm a daddy's girl.
Personally.

01:28:04.400 --> 01:28:06.100
Sorry.
I'm a daddy's girl.

01:28:06.130 --> 01:28:08.780
Which is which?
No?

01:28:08.800 --> 01:28:10.440
Okay.

01:28:10.520 --> 01:28:12.500
Congratulations.

01:28:12.530 --> 01:28:15.640
Go join the team.

01:28:19.720 --> 01:28:21.700
Congratulations to Pep.

01:28:21.730 --> 01:28:24.420
Well done to all
the Man City team yet again.

01:28:24.450 --> 01:28:28.340
Okay, next up, we go back
to our career awards.

01:28:28.370 --> 01:28:33.500
Our next career award is generously
sponsored by Audi Al Nabooda Automobiles.

01:28:33.530 --> 01:28:35.540
A big thanks to all the team there.

01:28:35.570 --> 01:28:38.060
And it goes to a player who really does

01:28:38.090 --> 01:28:46.340
epitomize inspiration, drive and that all
important, 'never say die' attitude.

01:28:46.370 --> 01:28:56.160
We honor the career,
ladies and gentlemen, of Casemiro.

01:29:03.120 --> 01:29:06.140
With speed, strength and power,

01:29:06.170 --> 01:29:10.180
Casemiro is one of the world's
leading central defensive midfielders.

01:29:10.210 --> 01:29:11.940
At club or international level.

01:29:11.960 --> 01:29:14.420
Casemiro has a defined role and he's

01:29:14.450 --> 01:29:19.500
a player whose physical attributes combine
seamlessly with guile and goal scoring.

01:29:19.530 --> 01:29:22.220
A player who thrives in the big moments.

01:29:22.250 --> 01:29:27.620
Casemiro has won an astonishing 25
trophies through his illustrious career

01:29:27.650 --> 01:29:32.920
of São Paulo, Real Madrid
and now Manchester United.

01:29:58.640 --> 01:29:59.540
Congratulations.

01:29:59.570 --> 01:30:03.360
I know you'd like to say
a few words in Portuguese.

01:30:08.640 --> 01:30:11.720
So, good evening.

01:30:12.160 --> 01:30:13.660
I will speak Portuguese.

01:30:13.690 --> 01:30:15.660
It's better for me.

01:30:15.690 --> 01:30:18.629
Thank you very much to everyone.

01:30:19.229 --> 01:30:21.680
It's a pleasure, thank you very much to
Dubai, Globe Soccer

01:30:22.614 --> 01:30:25.729
for this great event.

01:30:26.257 --> 01:30:28.014
Without a doubt, for me is
a pleasure to receive

01:30:28.214 --> 01:30:30.971
an award like this,
a great achievement in my career.

01:30:31.171 --> 01:30:35.671
I would like to thank my past clubs

01:30:35.871 --> 01:30:41.429
São Paulo, FC Porto, Real Madrid Castilla, Real Madrid,
and after Porto, Manchester United

01:30:43.700 --> 01:30:49.829
Without doubt, without them,
I wouldn't be able to win the titles I won.

01:30:50.229 --> 01:30:57.086
I wouldn't be able to win in my life,
and without doubt, I wouldn't be the person I am today.

01:30:57.250 --> 01:30:59.500
Thank you to my wife,
Anna Mariana,

01:30:59.530 --> 01:31:02.757
always with me in the
best and worst moments.

01:31:03.143 --> 01:31:04.714
But always with me.

01:31:04.886 --> 01:31:07.400
Once again,
Thank you all.

01:31:13.080 --> 01:31:15.980
Congratulations.
Enjoy the moment.

01:31:16.000 --> 01:31:17.460
I'm feeling slightly under pressure

01:31:17.480 --> 01:31:19.700
with the translation,
with so many portuguese speakers

01:31:19.730 --> 01:31:23.220
in the room, but Casemiro said
he's grateful for the recognition.

01:31:23.250 --> 01:31:30.780
Thanks to all the clubs he's represented
and dedicated the award to his wife Anna,

01:31:30.800 --> 01:31:34.800
who has been there throughout
and is with us this evening.

01:31:34.830 --> 01:31:38.740
He also said he's only 31 years old
and planning to win a whole lot more.

01:31:38.770 --> 01:31:41.100
Wouldn't doubt against it,
that's for sure.

01:31:41.130 --> 01:31:43.900
Okay, into the final few of the evening.

01:31:43.920 --> 01:31:45.600
Hope you've enjoyed the evening again down

01:31:45.630 --> 01:31:48.860
here at the Dubai Globe Soccer
Awards, live from Dubai.

01:31:48.880 --> 01:31:51.740
So, for clubs who have redefined the game

01:31:51.770 --> 01:31:55.260
of football, be that on the pitch or
of course, in the boardroom,

01:31:55.290 --> 01:31:58.460
the climb towards the pinnacle has been
consistent throughout,

01:31:58.490 --> 01:32:01.820
from planning and implementation
to the accomplishment of goals.

01:32:01.840 --> 01:32:06.860
None of this would have been possible
without the direction from the club

01:32:06.880 --> 01:32:11.580
president, who provides the blueprint as
to how clubs strike that perfect balance

01:32:11.610 --> 01:32:15.460
in the quest to become
a global football force.

01:32:15.490 --> 01:32:19.780
Over the last year, there have been clubs
who have taken their place in the upper

01:32:19.800 --> 01:32:24.140
echelons of the football world and clubs
who have consolidated their positions as

01:32:24.170 --> 01:32:28.660
global leaders all through the vision
and efforts of the president.

01:32:28.690 --> 01:32:33.720
Into your finalists then, for the best
president at the Nakheel Globe Soccer Awards.

01:32:34.114 --> 01:32:35.257
And the finalists are...

01:32:59.286 --> 01:33:02.200
The winner of the Dubai Globe Soccer Awards

01:33:02.286 --> 01:33:10.429
Best President
is Khaldoon al Mubarak of Manchester City.

01:33:19.120 --> 01:33:22.580
City's five trophies is
a testament to their growth.

01:33:22.600 --> 01:33:26.780
Under the leadership of Khaldoon al Mubarak,
Manchester City have embarked on a journey

01:33:26.800 --> 01:33:29.340
that has seen them
conquer all before them.

01:33:29.370 --> 01:33:33.920
With their president providing
the blueprint, City's seismic influence

01:33:33.950 --> 01:33:37.260
on the beautiful game
shows no sign of abating.

01:33:37.280 --> 01:33:39.780
Yeah, on the pitch, they continue
to reach new heights off it.

01:33:39.800 --> 01:33:41.700
They've just been a successful club,

01:33:41.730 --> 01:33:46.340
posting a Premier League record revenue
for the 22 to 23 financial year.

01:33:46.360 --> 01:33:48.420
With the City football group expanding its

01:33:48.450 --> 01:33:52.540
network to all corners of the globe,
a lasting legacy has been created.

01:33:52.570 --> 01:33:56.660
A 15 year journey and now City are
at the summit of world football.

01:33:56.690 --> 01:34:00.100
Khaldoon, maybe we can get
a few words with you.

01:34:00.130 --> 01:34:02.900
So many congratulations.

01:34:05.450 --> 01:34:11.380
We're talking about an era of dominance,
but sport has eras and peaks and droughts.

01:34:11.410 --> 01:34:16.380
So the question is, how long can
Manchester City keep this going?

01:34:16.410 --> 01:34:19.060
Well, allow me first to thank

01:34:19.090 --> 01:34:22.660
His Highness Sheikh Mansour Bin Mohammed
and Mattar Al Tayer

01:34:22.690 --> 01:34:25.340
and of course,
all the organizers for obviously this

01:34:25.370 --> 01:34:31.020
privilege to win this award.
And, you know, I accept the award...

01:34:31.050 --> 01:34:34.940
But to be honest, my job is not that hard.
When you have...

01:34:34.960 --> 01:34:37.060
We just gave you the big sell.

01:34:37.090 --> 01:34:39.460
When you have the best players

01:34:39.490 --> 01:34:45.660
in the world, when you have the best
coaching staff in the world, when you have

01:34:45.690 --> 01:34:50.380
the best organization
in the world, when you have the best

01:34:50.410 --> 01:34:55.020
football director, in Txiki Begiristain,
in the world when you have the best CEO,

01:34:55.050 --> 01:35:00.620
Ferran Soriano, in the world
and of course, having,

01:35:00.650 --> 01:35:02.660
and this is the best of all,

01:35:02.690 --> 01:35:06.580
the best owner in his
Highness Sheikh Mansour bin Zayed Al Nahyan

01:35:06.610 --> 01:35:11.100
in his unwavering support
and his positivity, always.

01:35:11.130 --> 01:35:12.260
And of course,

01:35:12.290 --> 01:35:18.100
all of this has to compensate
for a manager that's, I don't know,

01:35:18.130 --> 01:35:24.560
a bit average and of course the best
manager in the world in Pep Guardiola.

01:35:24.920 --> 01:35:30.420
And let's not forget what makes
Manchester City really special.

01:35:30.450 --> 01:35:32.820
We have the best fans in the world.

01:35:32.840 --> 01:35:41.460
So with all of this,
my job is pretty easy.

01:35:41.490 --> 01:35:44.020
How long can you keep him?
Pep?

01:35:44.050 --> 01:35:49.340
Listen, I didn't answer you the first
question, so let me just go back to that.

01:35:49.370 --> 01:35:51.260
How do you keep winning?

01:35:51.290 --> 01:35:58.700
You keep winning with
a commitment for excellence.

01:35:58.730 --> 01:36:01.340
When you wake up every day

01:36:01.370 --> 01:36:06.880
with that hunger, with that urge and when
it's consistent in the DNA and the culture

01:36:06.910 --> 01:36:11.540
of the club, one of the things I would say
I am most proud of is over this 15 year

01:36:11.570 --> 01:36:16.820
journey, what you have today
in Manchester City is a DNA,

01:36:16.840 --> 01:36:22.900
a culture that is in every person
that's involved in the club.

01:36:22.920 --> 01:36:24.540
And because of that,

01:36:24.570 --> 01:36:31.140
when you win 7 Premier leagues
in the last eleven years, when you win

01:36:31.170 --> 01:36:36.940
three Premier Leagues in a row,
the first team since 1991, 1999,

01:36:36.960 --> 01:36:41.020
to win a triple, the only other
team to win a triple in England.

01:36:41.040 --> 01:36:42.720
And this year, obviously we're going to go

01:36:42.750 --> 01:36:47.740
for hopefully the fourth Premier League
in a row and maybe another triple,

01:36:47.770 --> 01:36:55.860
but that hunger, that urge to get better,
to win, to constantly want to improve,

01:36:55.880 --> 01:37:00.740
never to be comfortable,
never to be content,

01:37:00.770 --> 01:37:04.860
this is, I think, what makes this
team and this organization special.

01:37:04.880 --> 01:37:09.060
This is what makes the 15 years,
I think, a privilege.

01:37:09.090 --> 01:37:12.900
But this is why I think you see
a consistency and this is why,

01:37:12.920 --> 01:37:16.900
when you look at the future,
I think from our perspective we're always

01:37:16.920 --> 01:37:21.300
looking at how to get better,
how to win more and how to constantly

01:37:21.330 --> 01:37:24.660
improve and that's going to be
how we build this legacy.

01:37:24.690 --> 01:37:29.820
Thank you.

01:37:29.840 --> 01:37:32.060
Since we forgot the question.
We can pass it.

01:37:32.090 --> 01:37:34.140
Ah, I love it.

01:37:34.170 --> 01:37:35.340
Great to speak to you.

01:37:35.370 --> 01:37:36.380
Congratulations.

01:37:36.410 --> 01:37:39.040
Thank you so much.

01:37:40.160 --> 01:37:42.740
Yeah, congratulations indeed to Khaldoon.

01:37:42.760 --> 01:37:44.420
Doing great to see you, as always.

01:37:44.450 --> 01:37:48.580
And well done yet again to all
the team behind Manchester City.

01:37:48.610 --> 01:37:50.380
Okay, on to the final awards

01:37:50.410 --> 01:37:55.420
of the evening as we gear up to our
climate, the conclusion of the evening

01:37:55.450 --> 01:38:00.260
next award has been generously
sponsored by our friends at Nakheel.

01:38:00.290 --> 01:38:02.700
Every single professional athlete was...

01:38:02.730 --> 01:38:04.660
Well, they started out as a dreamer.

01:38:04.690 --> 01:38:08.860
Recognition from their most loyal fans as
what the best in the business strive for.

01:38:08.880 --> 01:38:11.300
And there is no greater satisfaction

01:38:11.330 --> 01:38:16.540
for any footballer here or out there than
bringing smiles to the faces of fans.

01:38:16.570 --> 01:38:20.180
Fans from around the world,
quite literally,

01:38:20.210 --> 01:38:24.340
have cast their vote in the hope of seeing
their favorite footballer being crowned

01:38:24.370 --> 01:38:27.160
the Fans' Favourite Player of the Year

01:38:27.360 --> 01:38:30.629
Let's look into the finalists then.
And the finalists are...

01:38:56.960 --> 01:39:01.180
The Fans' Favourite Player of the year,
with an incredible

01:39:01.210 --> 01:39:12.920
5 million votes, is Cristiano Ronaldo.

01:39:20.920 --> 01:39:23.620
Cristiano Ronaldo continued to underline

01:39:23.650 --> 01:39:28.742
his status as one of the world's premier
athletes, winning the most Globe Soccer Awards

01:39:28.743 --> 01:39:34.240
since 2010, a testament
to his extraordinary talents.

01:39:34.960 --> 01:39:38.660
Historic move to Al-Nassr marks his
significant step in the evolution

01:39:38.690 --> 01:39:42.620
of Middle Eastern football and his
continued excellence on the field of play,

01:39:42.650 --> 01:39:47.880
his tribute to his unwavering
dedication to his craft.

01:39:49.120 --> 01:39:51.820
Ronaldo has a unique ability to captivate

01:39:51.840 --> 01:39:55.740
fans across the globe, drawing boasts
from every corner of the world.

01:39:55.770 --> 01:40:02.280
It's no surprise he's once again cemented
his status as the fans' favorite.

01:40:27.280 --> 01:40:31.000
Would you like to say a final few words?

01:40:34.320 --> 01:40:36.540
She asks very difficult questions.

01:40:36.570 --> 01:40:39.180
So, as you know,

01:40:39.210 --> 01:40:43.700
for me, the most important thing
in football, it's to make the fans happy,

01:40:43.730 --> 01:40:51.220
because it's the people who go to the
stadiums to see goals, to see good games.

01:40:51.250 --> 01:40:56.820
And if they vote, it's because
they have passion for football.

01:40:56.840 --> 01:41:01.540
For me, it's a special award because most
of the times we don't speak about

01:41:01.570 --> 01:41:07.780
the fans, but the stadiums without
the fans, if we go back two,

01:41:07.800 --> 01:41:13.820
three years ago, to the COVID, when we played
with the empty stadiums, it's no good.

01:41:13.840 --> 01:41:16.380
The people, if you ask the players,

01:41:16.410 --> 01:41:22.780
they don't enjoy, because, as I say,
without you guys, the football is nothing.

01:41:22.800 --> 01:41:27.520
So, thank you very much to voting on me

01:41:28.240 --> 01:41:36.600
and keep support the football and keep
support Al-Nassr and Cristiano.

01:41:40.360 --> 01:41:46.200
Congratulations, Cristiano Ronaldo,
ladies and gentlemen.

01:41:54.640 --> 01:41:59.580
And so, my friends, it comes
down to this, the grand finale.

01:41:59.610 --> 01:42:02.220
The final whistle is
just round the corner.

01:42:02.240 --> 01:42:03.980
Big thanks to all of you
for your patience.

01:42:04.000 --> 01:42:07.740
Big thanks to all the millions
that have tuned in around the world.

01:42:07.770 --> 01:42:09.660
So how do you round things off?

01:42:09.690 --> 01:42:14.060
Well, from the sublime to the magical
and all the way to the downright

01:42:14.090 --> 01:42:18.020
astonishing, superstars from around
the football world have really raised

01:42:18.050 --> 01:42:21.940
the standards the football loving
public were constantly glued to

01:42:21.960 --> 01:42:24.260
extraordinary action throughout the year.

01:42:24.290 --> 01:42:28.420
Defensive resilience, midfield
mastery goal scoring supremacy.

01:42:28.450 --> 01:42:32.780
It was a year which will
live long in the memory.

01:42:32.800 --> 01:42:35.100
Expectedly, some stars shone brighter

01:42:35.130 --> 01:42:38.780
and more consistently
delivered the spectacular.

01:42:38.800 --> 01:42:42.580
So it is time to crown
the best of the best.

01:42:42.610 --> 01:42:44.386
Your nominees are...

01:43:36.400 --> 01:43:40.679
It is quite the list, is it not?

01:43:40.680 --> 01:43:46.900
But one of those names has been crowned
the final winner of the evening.

01:43:46.920 --> 01:43:48.700
Behind this direction, please, ladies,

01:43:48.730 --> 01:43:53.540
gentlemen, honored guests,
Best Men's Player of the Year

01:43:53.570 --> 01:44:00.320
of this year's Nakheel
Dubai Globe Soccer Awards goes to...

01:44:04.080 --> 01:44:06.560
Erling Haaland.

01:44:14.160 --> 01:44:17.580
With a combination of power,
pace and intricate movement,

01:44:17.610 --> 01:44:22.520
Erling Haaland has scored against
some of the world's best defenses.

01:44:24.160 --> 01:44:26.300
With the tutelage of Pep Guardiola,

01:44:26.330 --> 01:44:29.100
Haaland scored a Premier League
record of 36 goals

01:44:29.130 --> 01:44:34.120
at 35 league appearances
in his debut season.

01:44:34.357 --> 01:44:40.213
Also finishes as the top scorer in Sydney's
triumphant run for the Champions League Glory with 12 goals.

01:44:40.214 --> 01:44:43.460
This once in a generation goalscorer is

01:44:43.490 --> 01:44:47.860
seamlessly fitted into a team
stacked with creative talents.

01:44:47.880 --> 01:44:54.120
His 50 goals in 2023 helps City
win five trophies in the year.

01:45:08.843 --> 01:45:11.519
So, the final award of the evening,

01:45:11.520 --> 01:45:14.500
the crowning glory.
The Best Men's Player of the Year at this

01:45:14.520 --> 01:45:16.360
year's Dubai Globe Soccer Awards
brought to you by

01:45:16.380 --> 01:45:18.671
Nakheel, Erling Haaland.

01:45:21.480 --> 01:45:22.580
Congratulations.

01:45:22.610 --> 01:45:25.860
Just a couple of words, if I may.

01:45:25.880 --> 01:45:32.260
It's almost easy to forget at times that
it was only last season you joined City.

01:45:32.290 --> 01:45:34.860
What is it about this club squad,

01:45:34.880 --> 01:45:40.640
this team that has made it so easy
for you to settle in and shine?

01:45:40.920 --> 01:45:44.520
Well, I think, first of all, the people,

01:45:45.000 --> 01:45:49.560
the guys that sit here is
a bunch of amazing people.

01:45:49.760 --> 01:45:55.820
And then you have the manager,
of course, who is not so bad as well.

01:45:55.840 --> 01:46:00.780
So, yeah, it's a fantastic club

01:46:00.800 --> 01:46:07.820
and the support we players get
from the administration and everything

01:46:07.840 --> 01:46:10.580
and the leaders in the club
is massive as well.

01:46:10.610 --> 01:46:15.900
So it's a nice club and I
really enjoy being there.

01:46:15.920 --> 01:46:17.140
Not a bad job at all.

01:46:17.160 --> 01:46:19.900
Have you still got the Champions League
as your ringtone on your phone?

01:46:19.920 --> 01:46:21.740
Now you've won it and done it?

01:46:21.770 --> 01:46:22.900
Yeah, I do.

01:46:22.920 --> 01:46:27.920
And I love this competition

01:46:28.040 --> 01:46:36.220
and, yeah, it was a big dream
when we won it and a fantastic feeling.

01:46:36.250 --> 01:46:38.780
Do you know when we're
going to see you back?

01:46:38.800 --> 01:46:40.860
I hope really soon because I'm getting

01:46:40.880 --> 01:46:45.100
a bit sick of not playing,
so hopefully soon.

01:46:45.120 --> 01:46:47.940
Great.
We wish you well with your recovery.

01:46:47.960 --> 01:46:51.060
Congratulations once again,
ladies and gentlemen.

01:46:51.090 --> 01:46:51.780
Erling...

01:46:51.800 --> 01:46:56.180
Oh, oh, hang on a minute,
I got a bit carried away.

01:46:56.210 --> 01:47:01.500
Before we let you go, we've got some
special messages from some of your fans.

01:47:01.530 --> 01:47:03.360
Just have a look.

01:47:10.840 --> 01:47:12.700
Congratulations, Haaland.

01:47:12.730 --> 01:47:14.740
Congratulations, Haaland.

01:47:14.770 --> 01:47:16.820
Congratulations, Haaland.

01:47:16.840 --> 01:47:19.880
Congrats, Haaland.

01:47:22.120 --> 01:47:23.540
Congratulations.

01:47:27.880 --> 01:47:31.400
"And Erling Haaland..."

01:47:37.200 --> 01:47:40.557
Congratulations, Haaland.

01:47:50.680 --> 01:47:53.480
Congratulations.

01:47:57.560 --> 01:47:58.580
Amazing.

01:47:58.610 --> 01:48:01.620
What does that mean when you see that?

01:48:01.650 --> 01:48:04.660
Of course, it's amazing.

01:48:04.690 --> 01:48:08.460
And what I also want to show
with my career is that no matter where you

01:48:08.490 --> 01:48:11.420
come from, I come from
a small town in Norway.

01:48:11.450 --> 01:48:14.000
You can come far.

01:48:14.080 --> 01:48:16.260
And, yeah, it's about hard work.

01:48:16.290 --> 01:48:19.420
It's about having the right
people around you.

01:48:19.450 --> 01:48:22.620
And, yeah, it's really beautiful to see.
Amazing.

01:48:22.650 --> 01:48:26.057
Congratulations once more,
ladies and gentlemen, Erling Haaland.

01:48:26.880 --> 01:48:28.340
Erling.
Congratulations to you.

01:48:28.360 --> 01:48:29.820
Erling, we're going to ask you to stay

01:48:29.840 --> 01:48:32.620
with us here on stage
as we round things up.

01:48:32.650 --> 01:48:34.500
Grab that trophy.

01:48:34.520 --> 01:48:35.900
Amanda, what an evening it has been.

01:48:35.920 --> 01:48:38.940
Another glorious evening right
here in the heart of Dubai.

01:48:38.960 --> 01:48:41.770
The magical setting of the Atlantis The Palm,

01:48:41.771 --> 01:48:44.260
where some of the world's
finest talents were honored.

01:48:44.280 --> 01:48:47.180
Yeah.
The 14th edition of the Globe Soccer Awards

01:48:47.210 --> 01:48:51.900
has delivered a spectacle we'd like
to call upon all of our winners to join,

01:48:51.920 --> 01:48:57.860
hurling up on stage to capture what
has been a truly magical evening.

01:48:57.880 --> 01:49:00.020
Yeah.
We would like you all now to sit back,

01:49:00.040 --> 01:49:02.240
appreciate and applaud
the star performers of 2023.

01:49:02.270 --> 01:49:07.200
A huge congratulations for the simply
incredible Cristiano Ronaldo.

01:49:07.230 --> 01:49:09.580
Please come and join us.

01:49:09.610 --> 01:49:13.900
We're also
going to welcome back onto stage

01:49:13.920 --> 01:49:19.120
the entire Manchester City
team, staff, all the winners.

01:49:19.120 --> 01:49:20.980
So, come on on, Man City,
let's get you back up.

01:49:21.000 --> 01:49:23.420
Including their coach, Coach of the Year,

01:49:23.450 --> 01:49:26.220
Pep Guardiola.

01:49:26.250 --> 01:49:29.660
Going to ask our Career Award
winners as well, of course.

01:49:29.680 --> 01:49:32.460
John Terry, can I ask you
to come and join us up here?

01:49:32.480 --> 01:49:34.120
We've got Lionel Scaloni with us as well.

01:49:34.150 --> 01:49:36.860
Lionel, I ask you to join us.

01:49:36.880 --> 01:49:38.860
And the brazilian Manchester United,

01:49:38.880 --> 01:49:41.700
Casemiro. Could ask you,
please, to join us.

01:49:41.730 --> 01:49:43.220
We would like to thank

01:49:43.250 --> 01:49:47.620
His Highness Sheikh Mansoor bin Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum,

01:49:47.650 --> 01:49:51.820
Chairman of the Dubai Sports Council,
and His Excellency Mattar al Tayer,

01:49:51.840 --> 01:49:58.220
Vice Chairman of the Dubai Sports Council,
for gracing us with their presence.

01:49:58.250 --> 01:50:03.620
We're calling on all of our winners here
tonight to join us up here on the stage.

01:50:03.640 --> 01:50:05.440
And a big thank you to each and every one

01:50:05.460 --> 01:50:09.020
of them taking their time out
of their busy schedules to be with us.

01:50:09.050 --> 01:50:10.180
Jorge, get up here.

01:50:10.210 --> 01:50:12.420
Come and join the party as well.

01:50:12.440 --> 01:50:14.340
As we say, a big thank you to all of our

01:50:14.370 --> 01:50:18.420
partners, all of our sponsors, and,
of course, each and every one of you.

01:50:18.450 --> 01:50:19.800
Amanda, bless you.
Thank you.

01:50:19.830 --> 01:50:22.780
It's been a great pleasure
to all those tuning in.

01:50:22.800 --> 01:50:26.060
Thank you.
We hope to see you here in Dubai next year

01:50:26.090 --> 01:50:29.140
and maybe in Sardinia
a little later on this year.

01:50:29.170 --> 01:50:31.820
From all the teams at Globe Soccer,

01:50:31.840 --> 01:50:34.300
specifically the
Dubai Globe Soccer Awards.

01:50:34.330 --> 01:50:41.529
From all of us here in Dubai, it is:
Good Night.

